/* =========================================================
   MAGIC ITEMS DATA
   Content for the "Magic Items" section, nested inside the
   "Items" dropdown in the Reference pane as a sibling of
   Equipment. This file holds ONE entry, MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA, whose
   own id/title ("items-magic-items" / "Magic Items") is appended
   as a child into #itemsContainer's .condition-list by
   dm-screen.js's renderDataDrivenReferenceSections(), rather than
   being rendered into its own top-level dropdown.

   Structure: MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA is a single entry whose "children"
   are category containers (Ammunition, Potions, Alchemical Items,
   Rings, Rods, Wands, Poisons, Staves), each of which has
   "children" that are rarity-bucket containers (Common, Uncommon,
   Rare, Very Rare, Legendary, Artifact), each of which has
   "children" that are the actual item entries. All container
   entries (the top-level entry, category containers, and rarity
   buckets) use an empty "html" field — only individual item
   entries carry real content.
   ========================================================= */

const MAGIC_ITEMS_DATA = {"id": "items-magic-items", "title": "Magic Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-ammunition", "title": "Ammunition", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-ammunition-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-unbreakable-arrow", "title": "Unbreakable Arrow", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This magic arrow doesn't snap, splinter, or otherwise get destroyed when it's used, so you can simply retrieve and reuse it after every shot instead of losing it the way ordinary ammunition is sometimes lost. Its one weakness is an antimagic field or similar effect: while inside one, the arrow loses its magic, and it can be broken like an ordinary arrow for as long as it remains there.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-walloping-ammunition", "title": "Walloping Ammunition", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Common</strong></p><p>This piece of magic ammunition is built to stagger a target rather than just wound it. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 10) or be knocked <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, on top of whatever damage the attack itself deals.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-1", "title": "Ammunition, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-2", "title": "Ammunition, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-ammunition-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ammunition-3", "title": "Ammunition, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This magic ammunition carries a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. That bonus is spent the instant the ammunition hits a target — once it deals damage, it reverts to an ordinary, nonmagical piece of ammunition.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ammunition-of-slaying", "title": "Ammunition of Slaying", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Any Ammunition), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This ammunition is crafted to bring down one particular kind of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a>, either chosen by the DM ahead of time or rolled randomly on the table below. Whenever it deals damage to a creature of that type, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. The instant it deals that extra damage, the ammunition burns out and becomes an ordinary, nonmagical piece of gear.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a></td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a></td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a></td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a></td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a></td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a></td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a></td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giants</a></td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-monstrosity\">Monstrosities</a></td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-ooze\">Oozes</a></td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a></td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a></td></tr></tbody></table><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Weapon (Arrow), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Called an arrow of slaying, this weapon is built to slay one particular kind of creature — as broad as an entire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">creature type</a> or as narrow as a single named race, chosen by the DM rather than rolled randomly (an arrow of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">dragon</a> slaying and an arrow of blue dragon slaying are both valid, for instance). Whenever it deals damage to a creature matching that type, race, or group, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take an extra 6d10 Piercing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Once it deals that extra damage, the arrow becomes an ordinary, nonmagical one. Bolts built the same way exist for crossbows, though the arrow form is by far the most common.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions", "title": "Potions", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-potions-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-potion-of-climbing", "title": "Potion of Climbing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a climbing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to climb.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing", "title": "Potion of Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>You regain 2d4 + 2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-plantspeak", "title": "Potion of Plantspeak", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Common</strong></p><p>This clear, brown liquid turns pale yellow once opened. Drinking it grants you the ability to communicate with <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a> for 5 minutes.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-willowshade-oil", "title": "Willowshade Oil", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Common</strong></p><p>A creature can use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to apply this dark blue oil to another creature that's been petrified for less than 1 minute, ending the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrified</a> condition at the start of what would be that creature's next turn.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-keoghtom-s-restorative-ointment-piccolo", "title": "Keoghtom's Restorative Ointment", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Ointment), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This glass jar holds 3 doses of a thick ointment that smells faintly of aloe. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, one dose can be swallowed or applied to the skin; the creature that receives it regains 2d8+2 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, stops being <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and is cured of any disease.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lesser-potion-of-mana", "title": "Lesser Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Drinking this deeply purple potion lets you regain 2 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 2 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 2 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-slipperiness", "title": "Oil of Slipperiness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it's wearing and carrying (one additional vial is needed for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes, after which the creature gains the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-freedom-of-movement\">Freedom of Movement</a> spell for 8 hours.</p><p>Alternatively, the oil can be poured on the ground as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, where it covers a 10-foot square and duplicates the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-grease\">Grease</a> spell in that area for 8 hours.</p><p>This sticky, black unguent is thick and heavy, but flows quickly when poured.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-advantage", "title": "Potion of Advantage", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this shimmering, golden potion, you gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> of your choice that you make within the next hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-animal-friendship", "title": "Potion of Animal Friendship", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you can cast the level 3 version of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a> spell (save DC 13).</p><p>Agitating this potion's muddy liquid brings little bits into view: a fish scale, a hummingbird feather, a cat claw, or a squirrel hair.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you can cast the animal friendship spell (save DC 13) for 1 hour at will. Agitating this muddy liquid brings little bits into view: a fish scale, a hummingbird tongue, a cat claw, or a squirrel hair.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-fire-breath", "title": "Potion of Fire Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>After drinking this potion, you can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to exhale fire at a target within 30 feet of you. The target must make a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 4d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The effect ends after you exhale the fire three times or when 1 hour has passed.</p><p>This potion's orange liquid flickers, and smoke fills the top of its container and wafts out whenever it is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-hill", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (hill)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 21 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 21 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-greater-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Greater Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You regain 4d4+4 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-growth", "title": "Potion of Growth", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “enlarge” effect of the Enlarge/Reduce spell for 10 minutes (no Concentration required).</p><p>The red in the potion's liquid continuously expands from a tiny bead to color the clear liquid around it and then contracts. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “enlarge” effect of the enlarge/reduce spell for 1d4 hours (no concentration required). The red in the potion's liquid continuously expands from a tiny bead to color the clear liquid around it and then contracts. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-greater", "title": "Potion of Healing (greater)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You regain 4d4 + 4 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-maximum-power", "title": "Potion of Maximum Power", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>The first time you cast a damage-dealing spell of 4th level or lower within 1 minute of drinking this potion, you can use the highest possible number on each of that spell's damage dice instead of rolling them.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-resistance", "title": "Potion of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one type of damage for 1 hour. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-swimming", "title": "Potion of Swimming", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed for 1 hour. During that time, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Strength (Athletics) checks you make to swim.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-water-breathing", "title": "Potion of Water Breathing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You can breathe underwater for 24 hours after drinking this potion. This potion's cloudy green fluid smells of the sea and has a jellyfish-like bubble floating in it.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Uncommon</strong></p><p>You can breathe underwater for 1 hour after drinking this potion. Its cloudy green fluid smells of the sea and has a jellyfish-like bubble floating in it.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-elixir-of-health", "title": "Elixir of Health", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you are cured of all magical contagions. In addition, the following conditions end on you: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>.</p><p>The clear, red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it cures any disease afflicting you, and it removes the blinded, deafened, paralyzed, and poisoned conditions. The clear red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-liquid-luck", "title": "Liquid Luck", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Indistinguishable from water by sight or smell, but tasting and smelling like the drinker's favorite fruit, this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Deception, Insight, and Persuasion checks for 3 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-dragon-s-bane", "title": "Oil of Dragon's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Oil), Rare</strong></p><p>This oil can coat a single weapon for 3 uses, or be used to dip up to 3 pieces of ammunition for 1 use each. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> that takes damage from a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in this oil takes an extra 6d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> of the same type from that attack. The oil dries and becomes inert after 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oil-of-etherealness", "title": "Oil of Etherealness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it's wearing and carrying (one additional vial is needed for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes. The affected creature then gains the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-etherealness\">Etherealness</a> spell for 1 hour.</p><p>Beads of this cloudy, gray oil form on the outside of its container and quickly evaporate.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-aqueous-form", "title": "Potion of Aqueous Form", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you transform into a pool of water, returning to your true form after 10 minutes or if you're Incapacitated or die. While transformed, you have a swimming Speed of 30 feet, can move over or through other liquids, can enter and occupy another creature's space, can shrink to fit through even Tiny openings, and extinguish any nonmagical flame you enter. You also have Resistance to nonmagical damage and Advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, but you can't talk, attack, cast spells, or activate magic items. Anything you're carrying that doesn't meld into your new form (such as armor you're wearing) continues to affect you as normal, but becomes inaccessible.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-clairvoyance", "title": "Potion of Clairvoyance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-clairvoyance\">Clairvoyance</a> spell (no <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a> required).</p><p>An eyeball bobs in this potion's yellowish liquid but vanishes when the potion is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-diminution", "title": "Potion of Diminution", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the “reduce” effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> spell for 1d4 hours (no Concentration required).</p><p>The red in the potion's liquid continuously contracts to a tiny bead and then expands to color the clear liquid around it. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-gaseous-form", "title": "Potion of Gaseous Form", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gaseous-form\">Gaseous Form</a> spell for 1 hour (no Concentration required) or until you end the effect as a Bonus Action.</p><p>This potion's container seems to hold fog that moves and pours like water.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to a set value for 1 hour, depending on which type of giant provided the fingernail sliver used to brew it — 21 for a Hill giant, 23 for a Frost or Stone giant, 25 for a Fire giant, 27 for a Cloud giant, or 29 for a Storm giant. The potion has no effect if your Strength is already equal to or higher than that value.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-fire", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (fire)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 25 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 25 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-frost-or-stone", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (frost or stone)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 23 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 23 or higher.</p><p>This version is brewed from either a frost giant's or a stone giant's fingernail, and both have the same effect. This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-superior", "title": "Potion of Healing (superior)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 8d4 + 8 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-heroism", "title": "Potion of Heroism", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain 10 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-temporary-hp\">Temporary Hit Points</a> that last for 1 hour. For the same duration, you are under the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-bless\">Bless</a> spell (no Concentration required).</p><p>This potion's blue liquid bubbles and steams as if boiling.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-invisibility", "title": "Potion of Invisibility", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's container looks empty but feels as though it holds liquid. When you drink the potion, you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This potion's container looks empty but feels as though it holds liquid. When you drink the potion, you become invisible for 1 hour. Anything you wear or carry is invisible with you. The effect ends early if you attack or cast a spell.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-invulnerability", "title": "Potion of Invulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>For 1 minute after you drink this potion, you have Resistance to all damage.</p><p>This potion's syrupy liquid looks like liquefied iron.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-mana", "title": "Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 4 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 4 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 4 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-mind-reading", "title": "Potion of Mind Reading", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> spell (save DC 13) for 10 minutes (no Concentration required).</p><p>This potion's dense, purple liquid has an ovoid cloud of pink floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-superior-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Superior Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 8d4+8 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-true-dreaming", "title": "Potion of True Dreaming", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Drunk before falling asleep, this poison-black liquid shows you, in your dreams, true visions of the past, present, or a possible future involving a creature, location, or object of your choosing. The DM determines the nature and duration of the visions.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thor-s-might", "title": "Thor's Might", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>This churning, deep blue liquid, shot through with white streaks, shakes and quivers in its container. For 1 minute after drinking it, any melee weapon attack you land lets out a thunderous crack, dealing an extra 1d6 Thunder <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. There's no limit to how many times this can trigger within the duration.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tincture-of-werewolf-s-bane", "title": "Tincture of Werewolf's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Rare</strong></p><p>Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature-type\">lycanthrope</a> that drinks this tincture must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be forced to change into its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> form, if it wasn't already in that form — while in that form, it can't change shape again for 24 hours. On a successful save, it takes only half the damage.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-oil-of-sharpness", "title": "Oil of Sharpness", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>One vial of this oil can coat one Melee weapon or twenty pieces of ammunition, but only nonmagical ammunition and Melee weapons that deal Slashing or Piercing damage are affected. Applying the oil takes 1 minute, after which it turns the coated weapon into a +3 Weapon or the coated ammunition into +3 Ammunition.</p><p>This clear, gelatinous oil sparkles with tiny, ultrathin silver shards.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-polymorph-potion", "title": "Polymorph Potion", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This almost-clear, pale green potion holds the floating, constantly-morphing projection of a creature. Drinking it lets you cast the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell on yourself for 15 minutes, without needing to maintain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">Concentration</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-continuous-healing", "title": "Potion of Continuous Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This murky red potion is highly sought after by soldiers and adventurers alike. After drinking it, you regain 2d10 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> at the start of each of your turns for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-enhanced-reactions", "title": "Potion of Enhanced Reactions", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This constantly color-shifting potion grants a +2 bonus to all <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 1 minute after you drink it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-flying", "title": "Potion of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain a Fly <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your Speed for 1 hour and can hover. If you're in the air when the potion wears off, you fall unless you have some other means of staying aloft.</p><p>This potion's clear liquid floats at the top of its container and has cloudy white impurities drifting in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-cloud", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (cloud)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 27 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 27 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-healing-supreme", "title": "Potion of Healing (supreme)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 10d4 + 20 Hit Points when you drink this potion. Whatever its potency, a Potion of Healing's red liquid glimmers when agitated.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-legendary-resistance", "title": "Potion of Legendary Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Highly sought after by spellcasters, this ink-black potion grants 2 uses of Legendary Resistance, letting you choose to succeed on a failed <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> instead, once per turn. Any unused charges last until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-longevity", "title": "Potion of Longevity", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your physical age is reduced by 1d6 + 6 years, to a minimum of 13 years. Each time you subsequently drink a Potion of Longevity, there is a cumulative 10 percent chance that you instead age by 1d6 + 6 years.</p><p>Suspended in this amber liquid is a tiny heart that, against all reason, is still beating. It vanishes when the potion is opened.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-possibility", "title": "Potion of Possibility", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this clear potion, you gain two Fragments of Possibility, each of which lasts 8 hours or until used. Whenever you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, or whenever an attack roll targets you, you can expend a fragment to roll an additional d20 and choose which of the d20s to use (if the original roll had <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a>, roll the extra d20 after that's been applied). While you hold one or more fragments from this potion, you can't gain another Fragment of Possibility from any source.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-protection", "title": "Potion of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This steel-grey, murky liquid is flecked with tiny beads of yellow, green, red, blue, purple, white, and black. Drinking it grants immunity to every <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-condition\">condition</a> for 1 hour except <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-grappled\">Grappled</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a>, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-restoration", "title": "Potion of Restoration", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion, full of floating strands of muscle, blood vessels, and organ matter, causes any of the drinker's destroyed or missing body parts and organs to regrow over the course of a week. The regrowth causes severe itching and occasional rashy pain at the site.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-revival", "title": "Potion of Revival", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>An entirely opaque, black potion with a single point of light hanging in its middle, this has no effect on a living creature. Poured down the throat of a creature that died within the last minute, it revives that creature to 1 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a>. It doesn't work on a creature that died of old age, and it can't restore any body part the creature was missing at the time of death.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-speed", "title": "Potion of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-haste\">Haste</a> spell for 1 minute (no Concentration required) without suffering the wave of lethargy that normally occurs when the effect ends.</p><p>This potion's yellow fluid is streaked with black and swirls on its own.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-supreme-healing-piccolo", "title": "Potion of Supreme Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>You regain 10d4+20 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when you drink this potion. It confers no benefit to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-truesight", "title": "Potion of Truesight", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this potion grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> out to a range of 120 feet for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-vitality", "title": "Potion of Vitality", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it removes any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> you have and ends the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition on you. For the next 24 hours, you regain the maximum number of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a> for any die you spend.</p><p>This potion's crimson liquid regularly pulses with dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, it removes any exhaustion you are suffering and cures any disease or poison affecting you. For the next 24 hours, you regain the maximum number of hit points for any Hit Die you spend. The potion's crimson liquid regularly pulses with dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-reincarnation-dust", "title": "Reincarnation Dust", "html": "<p><strong>Potion (Dust), Very Rare</strong></p><p>When this small pouch of purple dust is sprinkled onto a dead <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> or the remains of one, the dust is absorbed and, if the creature is willing, it returns to life with a new body as though the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-reincarnate\">Reincarnate</a> spell had been cast on the remains.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-superior-potion-of-mana", "title": "Superior Potion of Mana", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>Drinking this vibrant blue and purple potion lets you regain 8 points of a resource that recovers through short rests — 8 uses of Arcane Recovery for a Wizard, or 8 Sorcery Points for a Sorcerer.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vampiric-essence", "title": "Vampiric Essence", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This violently sour, vibrant green potion is among the most difficult to brew correctly — small mistakes can turn it into a bitter, poisonous concoction instead. Brewed correctly, for 1 minute after drinking it, a fifth of all Piercing, Slashing, or Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> dealt to you is instead absorbed and used to restore your own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">hit points</a>.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-potions-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-potion-of-giant-strength-storm", "title": "Potion of Giant Strength (storm)", "html": "<p><strong>Potion, Legendary</strong></p><p>When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes to 29 for 1 hour. The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is already 29 or higher.</p><p>This potion's transparent liquid has a sliver of a giant's fingernail floating in it.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items", "title": "Alchemical Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-blasting-powder", "title": "Blasting Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This volatile powder comes in a small pouch. Ignited by an open flame or a fuse, it explodes, and each <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> within 5 feet of it must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d6 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, or half as much on a success. Multiple pouches can be bound together to explode at once — each additional pouch adds 1d6 to the damage (maximum 10d6) and 5 feet to the blast radius (maximum 20 feet).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bottled-breath", "title": "Bottled Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This bottle holds a breath of elemental air. Inhaling it, you can either exhale it immediately or hold it. Exhaling grants the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> spell. Holding it means you don't need to breathe for 1 hour, though you can end that benefit early — for example, to speak — without gaining the gust of wind effect.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fake-blood", "title": "Fake Blood", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Crafted to look, smell, and taste exactly like real blood, this concoction only gives itself away to an Investigation check of 15 or higher, or to any level of identification magic.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-grenade-smoke", "title": "Grenade, Smoke", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, this grenade can be thrown up to 60 feet away, or up to 120 feet with a grenade launcher. One round after landing, it fills a 20-foot-radius area with smoke that's Heavily Obscured for 4 rounds in a moderate wind (at least 10 miles per hour), or just 1 round in a strong wind (20 miles per hour or more).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-common", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Common)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 1st through 3rd level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-muroosa-balm", "title": "Muroosa Balm", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>Made from the muroosa bush, this paste is known to prevent sunburn and resist fire. Spending 1 minute applying a quarter pint of it to your skin grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pepper-peppers", "title": "Pepper Peppers", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This fiery, crunchy snack grants 3 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> when eaten. Each batch produces 6 Pepper Peppers, and they can also be made with a cook's utensils.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-soothing-salve", "title": "Soothing Salve", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Common</strong></p><p>This sticky, sour-smelling salve is applied to a wound. For 1 hour after it's applied, spending a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Die</a> to recover hit points restores an extra 3 hit points per die spent.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-blight-ichor", "title": "Blight Ichor", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Distilled from a fungus native to the Blightshore badlands, this bitter, chartreuse liqueur grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Intelligence and Wisdom checks for 1 hour to any creature that drinks it, provided it's neither a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a> nor <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> — though it also carries a Vulnerability to Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> for the same duration. For each dose consumed, the drinker must also succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1d6 hours and suffer the effect of a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-confusion\">Confusion</a> spell for 1 minute. An <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> creature that drinks it instead gains Advantage on all Dexterity checks and immunity to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-brew-of-babel", "title": "Brew of Babel", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This baby-blue, highly opaque potion grants the ability to speak and understand — but not read or write — a language of your choice for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fire-balm", "title": "Fire Balm", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Applying a dose of this orange, herbal paste grants a +3 bonus to a single Constitution, Wisdom, or Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> made within the next 14 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-forgetfulness-antidote", "title": "Forgetfulness Antidote", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This moss-green liquid is brewed to counteract the Forgetfulness poison. Drinking it immediately ends all effects of that poison.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-greater-antitoxin", "title": "Greater Antitoxin", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, pumpkin-orange liquid grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on saving throws against Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 12 hours. During that time, the drinker also takes no damage over time from any poison, and can't be reduced to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> by poison damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-uncommon", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Uncommon)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 4th through 6th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-invisible-ink", "title": "Invisible Ink", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is invisible once written, becoming visible only to spells, traits, or items that reveal invisible things, or by applying a mild acid.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-life-s-liquor", "title": "Life's Liquor", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This strong pink liquid appears completely clear apart from the image of a red heart floating in its middle, which always seems to face the drinker no matter the angle. Drinking it grants 2d6+2 temporary <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-midnight-oil", "title": "Midnight Oil", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>When burned in a lantern, this oil sheds Bright Light out to 5 feet and Dim Light for another 5 feet, for 8 hours. A creature that stays within the light it sheds for the full 8 hours gains all the benefits of a Long Rest without needing to sleep, provided it only engages in light activity such as reading, studying, or talking during that time.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-murgaxor-s-elixir-of-life", "title": "Murgaxor's Elixir of Life", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Whoever drinks this concoction gains <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on death saving throws for 24 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pixie-dust", "title": "Pixie Dust", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can sprinkle this dust on yourself or another creature within 5 feet. The recipient gains a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 30 feet and the ability to hover for 1 minute. If the creature is airborne when the effect ends, it drifts safely to the ground, landing on its feet without taking damage. A packet holds enough dust for one use.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-pomander-of-warding", "title": "Pomander of Warding", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Once unwrapped, this ball of aromatic spices and perfumes fills a 15-foot-radius area with a strong scent for 24 hours. Any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 2 or lower that enters the area must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be turned, exactly as with a cleric's Turn Undead feature.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-quenching-philter", "title": "Quenching Philter", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This blue potion always has 2 ice cubes and 2 slices of lemon floating in it, and stays cool to the touch. Drinking it completely quenches thirst and removes the drinker's need to drink anything for 2 days, making it a favorite treat for travelers crossing arid country.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-soothsalts", "title": "Soothsalts", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystalline, lozenge-sized doses are consumed orally, leaving a telltale crimson stain around a frequent user's mouth. A dose grants <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Intelligence checks for 1d4 hours, but for each dose taken, the creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or gain a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> — an effect that stacks with multiple doses. Soothsalts can fetch up to 150 gp from the right buyer, but are illegal to trade in many places.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-bottled-rest", "title": "Bottled Rest", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This purple potion seems to hold clouds that continuously roll past the upper part of its container. Drinking it restores 3 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Dice</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-rare", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Rare)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 7th or 8th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-meditative-rest", "title": "Meditative Rest", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This vibrant orange liquid holds the vague images of two shapes locked in constant struggle. Drinking it restores 4 Ki Points.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tea-of-refreshment", "title": "Tea of Refreshment", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This warm drink removes one level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> from whoever drinks it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thessaltoxin-antidote", "title": "Thessaltoxin Antidote", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This potion changes color and texture every time it's looked at. Drinking it ends the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> effect imposed by Thessaltoxin.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-alchemical-items-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ink-spell-writing-very-rare", "title": "Ink, Spell Writing (Very Rare)", "html": "<p><strong>Alchemical Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This 1-ounce bottle of ink is used to write spells of 9th level into scrolls and spellbooks.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings", "title": "Rings", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-rings-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-jumping", "title": "Ring of Jumping", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-jump\">Jump</a> from it, but only on yourself, without expending a spell slot.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-mind-shielding", "title": "Ring of Mind Shielding", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you're immune to any magic that would let another creature read your thoughts, detect your alignment, or learn whether you're lying, and other creatures can communicate with you telepathically only if you allow it (you can end that welcome with a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>). If you die while wearing the ring, your soul immediately transfers into it, provided the ring isn't already holding one — you can then either linger there or move on to the afterlife. While your soul is in the ring, you can communicate telepathically with anyone wearing it, and that wearer can't block the contact the way a living creature normally could; they can use an action to release your soul if you're willing to go. To bring you back to life this way, someone needs to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-true-resurrection\">True Resurrection</a> targeting your soul while it's in the ring — successfully doing so uses up the ring.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-swimming", "title": "Ring of Swimming", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you have a swimming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> of 40 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-warmth", "title": "Ring of Warmth", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and you're comfortable in temperatures as low as −50 degrees Fahrenheit without needing extra protection. Wrap up in heavy clothing on top of that, and you can shrug off cold as extreme as −100 degrees Fahrenheit.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-water-walking", "title": "Ring of Water Walking", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this ring, you can stand on and move across any liquid surface — water, lava, acid, and the like — as though it were solid ground.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-animal-influence", "title": "Ring of Animal Influence", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge (Action) to cast one of the following spells: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a>; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fear\">Fear</a>, though it affects only <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a> and uses this ring's own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a> of 13 rather than your own spellcasting DC; or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-evasion", "title": "Ring of Evasion", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> while wearing it, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> and expend 1 charge to succeed instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-feather-falling", "title": "Ring of Feather Falling", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Whenever you fall while wearing this ring, you drift down at a rate of 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> when you land.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-free-action", "title": "Ring of Free Action", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> doesn't cost you extra movement, and magic can neither reduce any of your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speeds</a> nor give you the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-poison-resistance", "title": "Ring of Poison Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have Resistance to Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while wearing this ring.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-protection", "title": "Ring of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you get a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> and to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-resistance", "title": "Ring of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong></p><p>You have Resistance to one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-types\">damage type</a> while wearing this ring — Acid, Cold, Fire, Force, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, Psychic, Radiant, or Thunder — chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Resistance to one damage type, chosen by the DM or determined randomly when the ring is found.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-spell-storing", "title": "Ring of Spell Storing", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring can hold up to 5 levels' worth of prepared <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell\">spells</a> at once. Any creature can cast a spell of 1st through 5th level into the ring by touching it while casting — doing so has no effect beyond storing the spell, using up a share of the ring's capacity equal to the spell's level, and the spell stays there until it's cast from the ring or the ring is emptied. If the ring can't hold a spell being cast into it, that casting fails and is wasted. While wearing the ring, you can cast any spell stored inside it; doing so uses the original caster's spellcasting ability, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> bonus, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>, not your own, but is otherwise treated as you casting it. When found, this ring already holds 1d6 levels' worth of randomly determined spells chosen by the DM.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-the-ram", "title": "Ring of the Ram", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 to 3 of its charges to project a spectral ram's head at a target within 60 feet, making a ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack</a> with a +7 bonus. On a hit, the target takes Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> equal to 2d10 per charge spent, and if it's a creature, it must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be pushed back 5 feet per charge spent, unless it's too large or too firmly anchored to budge. Instead of attacking a creature, you can use this property to strike an object within range without needing an attack roll; doing so grants a +5 bonus to the Strength check needed to break that object for 1 charge spent, +10 for 2 charges, or +20 for 3 charges.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-x-ray-vision", "title": "Ring of X-ray Vision", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to see into and through solid matter for 1 minute, out to a range of 30 feet. Matter in that range looks transparent to you and doesn't block light — up to 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or 3 feet of wood or dirt; anything thicker blocks the vision, as does a thin sheet of lead. Using this property three or more times within a 24-hour period leaves you unable to see anything for 1d6 × 10 minutes afterward, as your eyes struggle to recover.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-regeneration", "title": "Ring of Regeneration", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you regain 1d6 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> every 10 minutes, as long as you have at least 1 hit point. If you lose a body part, it grows back over 1d6+1 days, provided you keep at least 1 hit point the entire time.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-shooting-stars", "title": "Ring of Shooting Stars", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring in <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dancing-lights\">Dancing Lights</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a> from it at will (action). The ring separately has 6 charges for two stronger properties, regaining 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn:</p><ul><li><strong>Faerie Fire.</strong> Expend 1 charge (action) to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a> from the ring.</li><li><strong>Ball Lightning.</strong> Expend 2 charges (action) to conjure 1 to 4 spheres of lightning, each about 3 feet across, in unoccupied spaces you can see within 120 feet — the more spheres you make at once, the weaker each one is individually. Each sheds <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> in a 30-foot radius and lasts as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on it (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 minute; you can move each one up to 30 feet as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, though never more than 120 feet from you. If a creature other than you comes within 5 feet of a sphere, the sphere discharges its lightning at that creature (DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> for half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, with the amount scaling to how many spheres you made at once) and then winks out.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-telekinesis", "title": "Ring of Telekinesis", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-telekinesis\">Telekinesis</a> from it at will, though you can target only objects that aren't currently being worn or carried by anyone.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rings-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-ring-of-djinni-summoning", "title": "Ring of Djinni Summoning", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can speak its command word (action) to summon a specific djinni from the Elemental Plane of Air into an unoccupied space you choose within 120 feet. It stays as long as you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-concentration\">concentrate</a> on sustaining the summons (as if concentrating on a spell), up to 1 hour, or until it drops to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, at which point it returns home. While summoned, it's friendly toward you and your companions and follows any commands you give it regardless of language; left uncommanded, it defends itself but takes no other actions. Once it departs, you can't summon it again for 24 hours, and if it ever dies, the ring loses its magic for good.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-elemental-command", "title": "Ring of Elemental Command", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This ring is bound to one of the four Elemental Planes — Air, Earth, Fire, or Water — chosen by the DM or determined randomly. While wearing it, you have Advantage on attack rolls against <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a> native to that plane, and they have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. As a Magic action, you can also target an elemental of that plane within 60 feet and force it to make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 18) or take the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> condition until the start of your next turn; while it's charmed this way, you control its movement and its action on your turn. The ring separately has 5 charges for casting spells tied to its element, regaining 1d4+1 expended charges daily at dawn, with a save DC of 18 for any of them that call for one:</p><ul><li><strong>Air.</strong> You can speak and understand Auran. When you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. You have Resistance to Lightning damage, and you have a flying <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-chain-lightning\">Chain Lightning</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wind-wall\">Wind Wall</a> (1 charge) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Earth.</strong> You can speak and understand Terran. Rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> for you, and you have Resistance to Acid damage. You can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, without disturbing the material you pass through; if you end your turn inside solid matter this way, you're shunted out to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire.</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you're immune to Fire damage. You can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water.</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan. You can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground, you can breathe underwater, and you have a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This version exists as four separately named rings — Ring of Air Elemental Command, Ring of Earth Elemental Command, Ring of Fire Elemental Command, and Ring of Water Elemental Command — each granting a modest baseline benefit simply for wearing it, plus a much stronger set of benefits that unlock only once you help slay an elemental matching the ring's element while attuned to it. Each version also lets you expend 2 of the ring's 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dominate-monster\">Dominate Monster</a> (DC 17) on an elemental of its matching type; the ring regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn.</p><ul><li><strong>Air (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Auran, and when you fall, you descend at only 60 feet per round and take no falling damage. <strong>Air (after helping slay an air elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Lightning damage and a flying Speed equal to your walking Speed, including the ability to hover.</li><li><strong>Earth (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Terran, and rubble, rocks, and dirt aren't Difficult Terrain for you. <strong>Earth (after helping slay an earth elemental).</strong> You gain Resistance to Acid damage, and you can move through solid earth or rock as though it were Difficult Terrain, being shunted to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied if you end your turn inside it; you can also cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stone-shape\">Stone Shape</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stoneskin\">Stoneskin</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-stone\">Wall of Stone</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Fire (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Ignan, and you have Resistance to Fire damage. <strong>Fire (after helping slay a fire elemental).</strong> Your Fire Resistance upgrades to immunity, and you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (3 charges) from the ring.</li><li><strong>Water (baseline).</strong> You can speak and understand Aquan, and you can stand on and move across liquid surfaces as though they were solid ground. <strong>Water (after helping slay a water elemental).</strong> You can also breathe underwater and gain a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-invisibility", "title": "Ring of Invisibility", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you can take an action to turn invisible, taking anything you're wearing or carrying with you. You stay <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> until you remove the ring, until you attack or cast a spell, or until you spend a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to become visible again.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-spell-turning", "title": "Ring of Spell Turning", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells. If you succeed on a save this way against a spell of level 7 or lower, that spell has no effect on you. If the spell also targeted only you, without creating any area of effect, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to hurl it back at its caster instead, who must then make their own saving throw against it, using their own spell save <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">DC</a>.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on saving throws against any spell that targets only you, without including you as part of a larger area of effect. If you roll a natural 20 on such a save and the spell is 7th level or lower, the spell has no effect on you at all, and instead targets its own caster — using that caster's slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability, exactly as though they'd cast it at themselves.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-ring-of-three-wishes", "title": "Ring of Three Wishes", "html": "<p><strong>Ring, Legendary</strong></p><p>This ring has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can take an action and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> from it. Once its last charge is spent, the ring loses its magic and becomes an ordinary ring.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods", "title": "Rods", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-rods-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-immovable-rod", "title": "Immovable Rod", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This flat iron rod has a button on one end. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can press the button to fix the rod magically in place — it doesn't move even if it's defying gravity, and holds up to 8,000 pounds of weight before deactivating and falling. Pressing the button again (an action, by you or anyone else) releases it. A creature can also free it by succeeding on a DC 30 Strength check.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-1", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-rulership", "title": "Rod of Rulership", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>As a Magic action, you can present this rod and command obedience from each <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> of your choice that you can see within 120 feet. Each target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> by you for 8 hours, treating you as its trusted leader. The effect on a target ends early if you or your allies harm it, or if you order it to act against its own nature. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-2", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-tentacle-rod", "title": "Tentacle Rod", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Rare</strong></p><p>Made by the drow, this magic weapon ends in three rubbery tentacles. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can direct each tentacle to attack a creature you can see within 15 feet of you, making a separate melee attack roll for each with a +9 bonus. Each tentacle that hits deals 1d6 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. If all three tentacles hit the same target, that target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or have its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> halved, gain <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Dexterity saving throws, and lose the ability to take <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reactions</a> for 1 minute; while affected this way, it can take either an action or a Bonus Action on its turn, but not both. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-absorption", "title": "Rod of Absorption", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this rod, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> when a spell that targets only you (and not an area including others) is cast, absorbing that spell's magic before it can affect you. Doing so doesn't store the spell itself, only the level of spell slot used to cast it, as points of stored energy — the rod can hold up to 50 points over its entire existence, and stops absorbing spells once that limit is reached, or if absorbing a spell's levels would push it over that limit. While attuned to the rod, a spellcaster can channel its stored energy into their own spell slots, up to 5th level, expending points equal to the slot's level to create it; a rod found already in play holds 1d10 points of stored energy.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-alertness", "title": "Rod of Alertness", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this rod, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls. You can also take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to cast one of the following spells from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-evil-and-good\">Detect Evil and Good</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-poison-and-disease\">Detect Poison and Disease</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-see-invisibility\">See Invisibility</a>.</p><p>As a Magic action, you can also plant the rod's haft in the ground, causing its head to shed Bright Light in a 60-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 60 feet. While within that bright light, you and your friendly creatures gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>, and can pinpoint the location of any Invisible hostile creature that's also within the bright light. This effect lasts 10 minutes, or until the rod is removed from the ground (a Magic action), and can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-security", "title": "Rod of Security", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this rod, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to activate it, instantly transporting yourself and up to 199 other willing creatures you can see into a paradise of your choosing that exists in an extraplanar space — a tranquil garden, a cheery tavern, an immense palace, a tropical island, or anything else you can imagine. The paradise always contains enough food and water to sustain its visitors, but anything else there can only exist there — an object taken outside the extraplanar space disappears. Every hour spent in the paradise restores <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">hit points</a> to a visitor as though it had spent one <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-point-dice\">Hit Point Die</a>, and no one ages while inside, though time still passes normally. Visitors can remain for up to 200 days divided by the number of creatures present (rounding down). Whoever activated the rod can end the effect early with an action, without needing the rod in hand to do so, sending everyone back to where they left from; the rod can't be activated again until the effect has ended.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-the-pact-keeper-3", "title": "Rod of the Pact Keeper, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>While holding this rod, you gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DCs</a> of spells you cast using your Warlock spell slots. In addition, once per day while holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to regain one expended Warlock spell slot; this property can't be used again until you finish a Long Rest.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-rods-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-rod-of-lordly-might", "title": "Rod of Lordly Might", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This rod normally functions as a magic mace with a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>. It also has six numbered buttons that you can press as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>; whichever function is currently active stays active until you press a different button, or press the same button again to return the rod to its normal form.</p><ul><li><strong>Button 1: Flame Tongue.</strong> The rod becomes a Flame Tongue of a bladed weapon type you choose.</li><li><strong>Button 2: Battleaxe.</strong> The rod becomes a magic battleaxe with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</li><li><strong>Button 3: Spear.</strong> The rod becomes a magic spear with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</li><li><strong>Button 4: Climbing Pole.</strong> The rod extends into a pole up to 50 feet long, capped with a spike and hooks that anchor it even in granite-hard surfaces, and sprouts a ladder of climbing bars spaced 1 foot apart along its length. It can support up to 4,000 pounds.</li><li><strong>Button 5: Battering Ram.</strong> The rod becomes a handheld battering ram, granting a +10 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to break through doors, barricades, and similar barriers.</li><li><strong>Button 6: Normal.</strong> Any other function ends, returning the rod to its normal mace form. While in this form, the rod also indicates magnetic north and gives you a rough sense of how deep underground or how high up you currently are.</li></ul>"}, {"id": "magic-item-rod-of-resurrection", "title": "Rod of Resurrection", "html": "<p><strong>Rod, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This rod has 5 charges, regaining 1 expended charge daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-heal\">Heal</a> from it (expending 1 charge) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-resurrection\">Resurrection</a> from it (expending all 5 charges). If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the rod disappears in a harmless burst of radiance.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands", "title": "Wands", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-wands-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-conducting", "title": "Wand of Conducting", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to conjure instrumental music or mimic the sound of a full orchestra for up to 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-pyrotechnics", "title": "Wand of Pyrotechnics", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to create a harmless burst of multicolored light at a point you can see within 60 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-scowls", "title": "Wand of Scowls", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to force a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> within 30 feet that you can see to scowl for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-smiles", "title": "Wand of Smiles", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Common</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to force a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> within 30 feet that you can see to smile for 1 minute.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-magic-detection", "title": "Wand of Magic Detection", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a> from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-magic-missiles", "title": "Wand of Magic Missiles", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (1st) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 3rd-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-secrets", "title": "Wand of Secrets", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to sense the presence and general direction of any secret door or trap within 30 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-web", "title": "Wand of Web", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (save DC 15) from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-1", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-binding", "title": "Wand of Binding", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-monster\">Hold Monster</a> (5 charges, save DC 17) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-person\">Hold Person</a> (2 charges, save DC 17) from it. You can also use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> and expend 1 charge to give yourself <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on a saving throw you're making against being <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a>, or on a check you're making to escape a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-grappling\">grapple</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-enemy-detection", "title": "Wand of Enemy Detection", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to speak its command word; for the next minute, you know the direction (but not the distance) of the nearest hostile creature within 60 feet of you. As long as the effect lasts, it ends early if you stop holding the wand.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-fear", "title": "Wand of Fear", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and point it at a creature you can see within 30 feet, expending 1 charge to force it to succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a>, if it has one, to move as far away from you as its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a> allows. Alternatively, you can expend 2 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fear\">Fear</a> (save DC 15) from it instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-fireballs", "title": "Wand of Fireballs", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (3rd) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 5th-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-lightning-bolts", "title": "Wand of Lightning Bolts", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend no more than 3 charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base (3rd) level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, up to a 5th-level casting for 3 charges.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (save DC 15) from it — 1 charge casts it at its base level, and each additional charge spent casts it one level higher, limited only by the wand’s own charge pool.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-paralysis", "title": "Wand of Paralysis", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and point it at a creature you can see within 60 feet, expending 1 charge to force it to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-paralyzed\">Paralyzed</a> for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-wonder", "title": "Wand of Wonder", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to choose a target within 120 feet you can see — a creature, an object, or a point in space — then roll 1d100 and consult the table below to discover what happens. If the effect casts a spell from the wand, that spell's save DC is 15, and its range becomes 120 feet if it isn't already that long or longer. If an effect covers an area, it must be centered on and include the target; if an effect has multiple possible subjects, the DM randomly determines which ones are affected.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–05</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>06–10</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-faerie-fire\">Faerie Fire</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td>You are <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> until the start of your next turn, believing something awesome just happened.</td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> on the target you chose. If you didn't target a creature, you instead take 1d6 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>26–30</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-stinking-cloud\">Stinking Cloud</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>31–33</td><td>Heavy rain falls in a 60-foot radius centered on the target. The area becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-lightly-obscured\">Lightly Obscured</a>. The rain falls until the start of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>34–36</td><td>An animal appears in the unoccupied space nearest the target. The animal isn't under your control and acts as it normally would. Roll again: on a 01–25 a rhinoceros appears, on a 26–50 an elephant appears, and on a 51–00 a rat appears.</td></tr><tr><td>37–46</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>47–49</td><td>A cloud of 600 oversized butterflies fills a 30-foot radius centered on the target. The area becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a>. The butterflies remain for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>50–53</td><td>You enlarge the target as if you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a>. If the target can't be affected by that spell, or if you didn't target a creature, you become the target instead.</td></tr><tr><td>54–58</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-darkness\">Darkness</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>59–62</td><td>Grass grows on the ground in a 60-foot radius centered on the target. If grass is already there, it grows to ten times its normal size and remains overgrown for 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>63–65</td><td>An object of the DM's choice disappears into the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-ethereal\">Ethereal Plane</a>. The object must be neither worn nor carried, within 120 feet of the target, and no larger than 10 feet in any dimension.</td></tr><tr><td>66–69</td><td>You shrink yourself as if you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a> on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>70–79</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>80–84</td><td>You cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a> on yourself.</td></tr><tr><td>85–87</td><td>Leaves grow from the target. If you chose a point in space, leaves sprout from the creature nearest to that point instead. Unless picked off, the leaves turn brown and fall off after 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>88–90</td><td>A stream of 1d4×10 gems, each worth 1 gp, shoots from the wand's tip in a line 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each gem deals 1 Bludgeoning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, and the total damage of the gems is divided equally among all creatures in the line.</td></tr><tr><td>91–95</td><td>A burst of colorful shimmering light extends from you in a 30-foot radius. You and each creature in the area that can see must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</td></tr><tr><td>96–97</td><td>The target's skin turns bright blue for 1d10 days. If you chose a point in space, the creature nearest to that point is affected instead.</td></tr><tr><td>98–00</td><td>If you targeted a creature, it must make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>; if you didn't target a creature, you become the target and make the save instead. Failing by 5 or more instantly <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-petrified\">Petrifies</a> the target; any other failure leaves it <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> and beginning to turn to stone, forcing it to repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on another failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until removed by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell or similar magic.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-2", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-polymorph", "title": "Wand of Polymorph", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>This wand has 7 charges and regains 1d6+1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend its last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> (save DC 15) from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-wand-of-the-war-mage-3", "title": "Wand of the War Mage, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a spellcaster)</p><p>While holding this wand, you gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spell-attack\">spell attack rolls</a>. In addition, you ignore Half <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-half-cover\">Cover</a> when making a spell attack.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wands-artifact", "title": "Artifact", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-wand-of-orcus", "title": "Wand of Orcus", "html": "<p><strong>Wand, Artifact</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Made from a demon lord's own bones and topped with an enlarged human skull, this wand can be wielded as a magic mace with a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a>, dealing an extra 2d12 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> on a hit. It also grants a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> while held.</p><p>Any creature other than Orcus himself that attempts to attune to the wand must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or die and rise as a Zombie under the wand's control; even on a success, the creature takes 10d6 Necrotic damage.</p><p>The wand has 7 charges, regaining 1d4+3 expended charges daily at dawn (Orcus himself, or a follower he's blessed, spends 2 fewer charges — minimum 0 — for the same spells). While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend charges to cast one of the following spells (save DC 18) from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animate-dead\">Animate Dead</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-dead\">Speak with Dead</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-blight\">Blight</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-circle-of-death\">Circle of Death</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-finger-of-death\">Finger of Death</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-power-word-kill\">Power Word Kill</a> (4 charges).</p><p>Separately, once per day, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to conjure Skeletons and Zombies totaling up to 500 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a> worth of undead (each with average hit points), rising from the ground or forming in unoccupied spaces within 300 feet of you. They obey your commands until destroyed or until the next dawn, when they collapse into inanimate piles of bone and rotting flesh.</p><p>Like other artifacts, the wand carries its own set of random beneficial and detrimental properties (2 minor and 1 major of each) determined when it's introduced to the campaign; its detrimental properties are suppressed while it's attuned to Orcus himself.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons", "title": "Poisons", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-poisons-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-acid-tablets", "title": "Acid Tablets", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>Disguised as ordinary stomach tablets, these force a creature who swallows one to make a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d6 Acid <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and be unable to vomit for 30 seconds. At the start of each of its turns after that, the creature repeats the save; success lets it throw up and rid itself of the poison.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-basic-poison", "title": "Basic Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Common</strong></p><p>This vial of poison can coat one slashing or piercing weapon, or up to three pieces of ammunition; applying it takes an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>. A <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-creature\">creature</a> hit by the coated weapon or ammunition must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Once applied, the poison stays potent for 1 minute before drying out.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-biza-s-breath", "title": "Biza's Breath", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>A creature exposed to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 minute. While poisoned this way, it must use its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make a melee attack against a randomly determined creature within its reach, or do nothing on its turn if no other creature is in reach. It can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dazzling-bomb", "title": "Dazzling Bomb", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>Set off by a fuse or tripwire, this small bomb fills a 30-foot-diameter sphere with a highly irritating powder. Creatures caught in the powder must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be Stunned for 1 turn. <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-liquid-paranoia", "title": "Liquid Paranoia", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Common</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison gains the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> condition, with the source of its fear being the next <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> it sees within 5 minutes of drinking it. The creature must make a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>; on a failure, the fear lasts 1 hour, or half as long on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-nausea-pellet", "title": "Nausea Pellet", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Common</strong></p><p>This black pellet can be thrown as an improvised weapon with a 20/40 range. On impact, it shatters into a fine powder filling a 5-foot square. Creatures in that square must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 30 seconds, repeating the save at the end of each of their turns. A poisoned creature can also use its action, or a Bonus Action while holding a Stomach Stopper, to throw up and end the poison early. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-perfume-of-bewitching", "title": "Perfume of Bewitching", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Common</strong></p><p>This tiny vial holds enough magic perfume for one use. As an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a>, you can apply it to yourself; for 1 hour afterward, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Charisma checks directed at <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a> of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-challenge-rating\">challenge rating</a> 1 or lower, and those affected don't realize they've been magically influenced.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-angel-s-powder", "title": "Angel's Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine, bright white powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or, for 1 hour, perceive everyone around it as trusted friends, becoming extremely suggestible to non-aggressive persuasion and deception.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-assassin-s-blood", "title": "Assassin's Blood", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must make a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 6 (1d12) Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage and isn't Poisoned.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-bane-berry-extract", "title": "Bane Berry Extract", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>A creature that swallows this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, it has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Strength, Constitution, and Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> for 15 minutes. On a successful save, the target feels no effect at all.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-black-paste", "title": "Black Paste", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact via clothing), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Designed to resemble leather or boot polish, this poison shines like new once applied to a piece of clothing. Wearing the treated garment for a total of 12 hours (not necessarily consecutive) forces a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the wearer takes 1d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. Unless the poisoned garment is removed, the saving throw repeats every 12 hours for the next 3 months.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-directed-delay", "title": "Directed Delay", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This thick black liquid, viscous as concentrated molasses, is delivered through a wound or injection. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or suffer the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-slow\">Slow</a> spell, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns. On a successful save, its movement Speed is instead reduced by 5 feet for 3 turns.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-lava-paste", "title": "Lava Paste", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This mundane-looking yellowish paste is applied to skin or clothing. The target must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d6 Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and become Vulnerable to fire damage for the next 12 hours; on a success, it takes half damage and avoids the vulnerability.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-malice", "title": "Malice", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Blinded conditions for 1 hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-noxious-transpiration", "title": "Noxious Transpiration", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This pale turquoise poison isn't dangerous to drink by itself, but starting 2 hours after ingestion, the drinker's sweat turns poisonous for 1 hour. Any contact with a patch of the drinker's skin roughly palm-sized or larger forces the toucher to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d10+4 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success avoids the damage entirely. Once a creature is exposed and takes no damage, it can't be affected by that dose again for 12 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-pale-tincture", "title": "Pale Tincture", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 250 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition. The Poisoned creature repeats the save every 24 hours, taking another 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each failure; none of this damage can be healed by any means while the creature remains Poisoned. After seven successful saves, the creature is no longer Poisoned and can heal normally.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-philter-of-love", "title": "Philter of Love", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking this potion, you are <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-charmed\">Charmed</a> by that creature and have the Charmed condition for 1 hour.</p><p>This rose-hued, effervescent liquid contains one easy-to-miss bubble shaped like a heart.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking this philter, you become charmed by that creature for 1 hour. If the creature is of a species and gender you are normally attracted to, you regard it as your true love while you are charmed. This potion's rose-hued, effervescent liquid contains one easy-to-miss bubble shaped like a heart.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-potion-of-poison", "title": "Potion of Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This concoction looks, smells, and tastes exactly like a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"magic-item-potion-of-healing\">Potion of Healing</a> or other beneficial potion — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell reveals its true nature. Drinking it deals 4d6 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> condition for 1 hour.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This concoction looks, smells, and tastes exactly like a Potion of Healing or other beneficial potion — only an Identify spell reveals its true nature. Drinking it deals 3d6 Poison damage and forces a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or the Poisoned condition; while poisoned this way, the drinker takes another 3d6 Poison damage at the start of each of its turns and can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, with each successful save reducing the damage taken on subsequent turns by 1d6 until it reaches 0.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-serpent-venom", "title": "Serpent Venom", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated giant poisonous snake. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or take 3d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-taratella-the-great-humiliator", "title": "Taratella: The Great Humiliator", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This murky, muddy brown liquid forces the drinker to succeed on a DC 14 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> indefinitely. While poisoned this way, the target experiences vivid dreams and occasional hallucinations of onlookers laughing at it, taking 1d4+1 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> every 6 hours. On a successful save, the target is instead poisoned for 2 days, taking only 2 Psychic damage every 6 hours. The only known cure is to dance as poorly as possible for 1 hour in a town square during daylight.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-truth-serum", "title": "Truth Serum", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 150 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and be unable to speak a deliberate lie for 1 hour.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "equipment-burnt-othur-fumes", "title": "Burnt Othur Fumes", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, then repeat the saving throw at the start of each of its turns, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage on each further failure. The poison ends after three successful saves.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-devil-s-powder", "title": "Devil's Powder", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This hyper-fine red powder is blown into a target's face before dispersing harmlessly. The target must succeed on a DC 18 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or perceive the world for 1 hour as a hellscape crawling with foul creatures, becoming extremely susceptible to intimidation, aggressive persuasion, and deception during that time. On a successful save, the target instead feels only mild paranoia and skittishness.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dracula-s-essence", "title": "Dracula's Essence", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Kept as a small vial of what looks like fresh blood, this poison turns to a still, rust-colored liquid once opened. If drunk, or if it enters the bloodstream through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or immediately vomit up everything in its stomach and take 2d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becoming unable to sleep; on a success, it instead vomits and takes 2d8 Poison damage. An hour later, the target becomes supremely sensitive to direct sunlight, taking 1d4 Fire damage for every minute it spends outside of shade while not wearing Muroosa Balm, and craves nothing but raw meat and blood (especially its own species') — trying to eat or drink anything else forces it to vomit and take 1d6 Poison damage. Each hour it goes without raw meat or blood, it gains 1 level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>. These effects last 24 hours.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-drider-poison", "title": "Drider Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>Harvested directly from a drider rather than brewed, this venom forces a creature hit by a weapon or piece of ammunition coated in it to succeed on a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 hour. If the save fails by 5 or more, the target is also <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-unconscious\">Unconscious</a> while poisoned this way. The target wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-essence-of-ether", "title": "Essence of Ether", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled)</strong> &middot; Cost 300 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 8 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-fire-plague", "title": "Fire Plague", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>This rose-orange powder is baked into bread or pastry. Eating at least a quarter of the treated food forces a DC 14 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the eater takes 1d6 Fire and 1d6 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>, becomes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>, and develops necrotic patches across its skin. While poisoned this way, it suffers vivid hallucinations of death and dying, and can remake the saving throw each morning; a success ends all the effects.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-forgetfulness", "title": "Forgetfulness", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Rare</strong></p><p>This fine, lavender powder forces anyone who breathes it in to succeed on a DC 14 Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a>. While poisoned this way, the target has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Intelligence <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> and checks, and must succeed on a DC 7 Intelligence check whenever it tries to recall anything that happened 4 or more weeks ago. It can repeat the saving throw at the start of every morning, ending the effect on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-lolth-s-sting", "title": "Lolth's Sting", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Drow Poison.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it also falls Unconscious for the same duration. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-magebane", "title": "Magebane", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Rare</strong></p><p>Smelling of old boots despite its red-wine appearance, this poison grants the drinker the benefit of the Mage Slayer feat for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-magic-s-bane", "title": "Magic's Bane", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>This clear, colorless poison holds a purple, cloudy sphere that darts through it. Once it enters a creature's bloodstream, the target must succeed on a DC 14 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or its ability to cast spells is disrupted for 1 minute, requiring a successful DC 10 Arcana check each time it tries to cast one anyway; a success avoids the disruption entirely. The saving throw can be repeated at the end of each of the target's turns.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-oil-of-taggit", "title": "Oil of Taggit", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 400 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Unconscious conditions for 24 hours. The creature wakes up if it takes damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-thessaltoxin", "title": "Thessaltoxin", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Rare</strong></p><p>First distilled from the blood of the artificer Thessalar, this poison forces a creature struck by it to succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take on a new form as if affected by the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> spell — a random beast, or a creature it's seen within the last 24 hours, chosen by the DM. The transformation lasts until the end of the target's next long rest, and isn't cured by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a>, though a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell restores the creature's true form.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-torpor", "title": "Torpor", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition and have its Speed halved for 4d6 hours.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 600 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Incapacitated conditions for 4d6 hours.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armourer-s-blight", "title": "Armourer's Blight", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This harmless-seeming, pale green liquid is designed to turn armor into a death trap. Poured, smeared, or thrown onto a piece of armor, it seeps into the metal and forces the wearer to succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> at the start of each of its turns or take 4d6 Lightning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>; a success reduces the damage to 4. The poison lasts for 10 years and can only be removed by heating the metal to at least 700°F/1300°F.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-black-thistle-poison", "title": "Black Thistle Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact, Injury, Ingested via fumes), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This jet-black poison, suspended with metallic cobalt mica-like powder, releases faint purple fumes for up to 30 minutes once its ampule is opened, filling a 10-foot cube. Applied to weapons or up to 10 pieces of ammunition, it stays active for 30 minutes (or 3 minutes on ammunition), continuing to give off the same fumes during that time.</p><p>Exposure to the fumes for more than 12 seconds forces a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature takes 4 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> for 30 seconds (2 Necrotic damage on a success); repeated brief exposure has no further effect for 12 hours. Exposure for 5 minutes or more in a day instead forces a DC 16 Constitution save, dealing 2d8 Necrotic damage and Blinding the creature for 5 days on a failure (half damage, no blindness on a success); a second cumulative 5 minutes of exposure deals 2d12 Necrotic damage and Blinds the creature permanently, curable only by regeneration magic or a potion, with no saving throw. Direct contact with the poison itself (blood or injection) is far more dangerous: a DC 18 Constitution save against 15+ minutes of fuming exposure, with a failure dealing 5d12 Necrotic damage and permanently Blinding and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafening</a> the creature, ruining its sense of smell and taste, and reducing its sense of touch by 80% for the rest of its life, with severe ongoing pain reducible only by regenerative magic or repeated Potions of Restoration; a success still deals 3d8 Necrotic damage and costs a sense (DM's choice) or reduces touch by 35% for 12 hours, curable the same way or with regenerative magic of a lower level.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-carrion-crawler-mucus", "title": "Carrion Crawler Mucus", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated carrion crawler. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned and Paralyzed conditions for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns to end the effect early.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Contact)</strong> &middot; Cost 200 GP per dose</p><p>Called \"Crawler Mucus.\" A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-coup-de-poudre", "title": "Coup de Poudre", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Made from herbs, powdered human bones, and animal poisons, this concoction is the first step in turning a living <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoid</a> into a loyal Revenant. If ingested, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 5d8 Necrotic and 5d8 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and fall into a death-like state at the stroke of midnight (half damage and no death-state on a success). A creature reduced to 0 hit points this way must be buried within 3 days and exhumed within 8 hours of burial, after which a 4-hour ritual binds its captured soul to the poisoner in a sealed jar; the body then reanimates as a Revenant that follows only verbal commands (given as a Bonus Action) in a language it understood in life, healing to full whenever it's midnight while the jar stays sealed and intact.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-deathsleep", "title": "Deathsleep", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>A creature that ingests this poison must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 24 hours, appearing dead for the duration. Only a successful DC 20 Medicine check can determine that the creature is merely poisoned rather than truly dead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-essence-of-rage", "title": "Essence of Rage", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This muddy brown poison turns bright, violent red when agitated with more than the lightest touch. Drinking it grants the Barbarian class's Rage feature for 30 seconds. If instead introduced through a wound or injection, the target must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or be forced into that same Rage for 30 seconds, compelled to attack the nearest target with melee attacks; on a success, it gains the benefit of Rage voluntarily for 60 seconds instead. A forced target can attempt another saving throw starting on its second turn under the effect, ending it on a success. This poison has no effect on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-medusa-s-vengeance", "title": "Medusa's Vengeance", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This thick, grey poison is applied to weapons or ammunition, remaining active for 5 minutes on a weapon or 3 days on up to 20 pieces of ammunition (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> are unaffected by it). The third time a coated weapon draws blood from the same target, that target must succeed on a DC 16 Charisma <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or begin petrifying: it loses 5 feet of Speed at the start of each of its next 3 turns and, over the following 15 minutes, becomes increasingly sluggish before turning fully to stone. Once a target succeeds on the saving throw, it's immune to this poison for the next minute.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-midnight-tears", "title": "Midnight Tears", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,500 GP per dose</p><p>A creature that ingests this poison suffers no effect until the stroke of midnight. If the poison hasn't been neutralized by then, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or take 9d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-night-hag-s-curse", "title": "Night Hag's Curse", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Ingested, Injury), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Meant to torment rather than kill, this clear, lilac poison forces a target who ingests it or has it injected into their blood to succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, the target suffers vivid nightmares for a week, taking 4 Psychic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> each morning upon waking. On a failure, the target's mind is permanently afflicted: it experiences night terrors that deal 2d10 Psychic damage upon waking each morning, and no longer automatically clears a level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a> by completing a long rest — instead, the target rolls 1d100 each morning, restoring the level only on a 25 or lower, gaining a level instead on a 75 or higher, and seeing no change in between. The only cure is a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-greater-restoration\">Greater Restoration</a> spell of 6th level or higher, cast after the target drinks a Tea of Refreshment while it has no levels of Exhaustion.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sandman-s-revenge", "title": "Sandman's Revenge", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Inhaled), Very Rare</strong></p><p>This yellowish, chunky powder is blown into a target's face. On contact, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 2d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and gain 3 levels of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>; on a success, it takes 4 Necrotic damage and gains only 1 level of Exhaustion. Holding one's breath doesn't help, since the powder targets the nasal membranes; <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> are unaffected.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-water-of-death", "title": "Water of Death", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury, Ingested), Very Rare</strong></p><p>Looking, smelling, and tasting exactly like water, this poison defies even most magical and alchemical tests — only an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell cast at 7th level or higher, or 24 hours of detailed alchemical testing costing 300 gp, reveals what it truly is. Any contact with it forces a DC 20 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or the creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-blinded\">Blinded</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> for 48 hours and too wracked with pain to move for 24 hours, its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Point</a> maximum permanently reduced by 2d12 before it takes 7d10 Poison <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> 12 hours later. On a successful save, its hit point maximum is still permanently reduced by 2d12, and it has blurred vision and muffled hearing for 24 hours. The lost hit point maximum can only be restored by healing after drinking a Potion of Vitality, or by a Greater Restoration or Regenerate spell cast at 8th level or higher.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-poisons-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "equipment-purple-worm-poison", "title": "Purple Worm Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 21 Constitution saving throw or take 10d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 2,000 GP per dose</p><p>Must be harvested from a dead or incapacitated purple worm. A creature subjected to it must succeed on a DC 19 Constitution saving throw or take 12d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}, {"id": "equipment-wyvern-poison", "title": "Wyvern Poison", "html": "<p><strong>Poison (Injury)</strong> &middot; Cost 1,200 GP per dose</p><p>A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or take 7d6 Poison damage, or half as much damage on a successful save.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves", "title": "Staves", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-staves-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-adornment", "title": "Staff of Adornment", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>If you place an object weighing no more than 1 pound (such as a shard of crystal, an egg, or a stone) above the tip of the staff while holding it, the object floats an inch above the staff's tip and remains there until it is removed or until the staff leaves your possession. The staff can have up to three such objects floating above its tip at any given time. While holding the staff, you can cause one or more of the floating objects to slowly spin or turn in place.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-birdcalls", "title": "Staff of Birdcalls", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>This wooden staff is decorated with bird carvings. It has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to create one of the following sounds out to a range of 60 feet: a finch's chirp, a raven's caw, a duck's quack, a chicken's cluck, a goose's honk, a loon's call, a turkey's gobble, a seagull's cry, an owl's hoot, or an eagle's shriek. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff explodes in a harmless cloud of feathers and is lost forever.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-flowers", "title": "Staff of Flowers", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Common</strong></p><p>This wooden staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cause a flower to sprout from a patch of earth or soil within 5 feet of you, or from the staff itself. Unless you choose a specific kind of flower, the staff creates a mild-scented daisy. The flower is harmless and nonmagical, and it grows or withers as an ordinary flower would. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff turns into flower petals and is lost forever.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-adder", "title": "Staff of the Adder", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>You can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to speak this staff's command word, causing the head of the staff to become that of an animate poisonous snake for 1 minute. By using another Bonus Action to speak the command word again, you return the staff to its normal, inanimate form. Using the snake head, you can make a melee <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-action\">attack</a> against a target within the staff's 5-foot reach, adding your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-proficiency\">Proficiency</a> Bonus to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a>. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 Piercing <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> and must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 3d6 Poison damage. While animate, the snake head can be attacked; it has an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">AC</a> of 15 and 20 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. If it drops to 0 Hit Points, the staff is destroyed. As long as the staff isn't destroyed, the snake head regains all its lost Hit Points when it reverts to its inanimate form.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-python", "title": "Staff of the Python", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>You can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to speak this staff's command word and throw the staff on the ground within 10 feet of you. The staff becomes a Giant Constrictor Snake under your control and acts on its own initiative count in combat. By using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to speak the command word again, you return the staff to its normal form in a space formerly occupied by the snake. On your turn, you can mentally command the snake if it's within 60 feet of you and you aren't <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> — you decide what action the snake takes and where it moves on its next turn, or you can issue it a general command, such as to attack your enemies or guard a location. If the snake is reduced to 0 Hit Points, it dies, reverts to its staff form, and the staff then shatters and is destroyed. If the snake reverts to its staff form before losing all its Hit Points, it regains all of them.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-charming", "title": "Staff of Charming", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 charge to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-charm-person\">Charm Person</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-command\">Command</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-comprehend-languages\">Comprehend Languages</a> from it, using your spell save DC. The staff can also be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff. If you're holding it and fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, you can turn that failed save into a success; once you do so, you can't use this property again until the next dawn. If you succeed on a save against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, with or without the staff's help, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to expend 1 charge and turn the spell back on its caster as if you had cast it yourself. The staff regains 1d8+2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-healing", "title": "Staff of Healing", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, or Druid)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spellcasting ability: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cure-wounds\">Cure Wounds</a> (1 charge per spell level, up to 4th), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lesser-restoration\">Lesser Restoration</a> (2 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mass-cure-wounds\">Mass Cure Wounds</a> (5 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff vanishes in a flash of light and is lost forever.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-swarming-insects", "title": "Staff of Swarming Insects", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff has 10 charges and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, a swarm of insects consumes and destroys the staff, then disperses. While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend some of its charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-giant-insect\">Giant Insect</a> (4 charges) or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-insect-plague\">Insect Plague</a> (5 charges) from it, using your spell save DC. You can also take an action and expend 1 charge to cause a swarm of harmless flying insects to spread out from you in a 30-foot radius; the swarm moves with you, remains for 10 minutes, and makes its area <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a> for any creature but you. A wind of at least 10 miles per hour disperses the swarm and ends the effect.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-woodlands", "title": "Staff of the Woodlands", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. While holding it, you have a +2 bonus to spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 6 charges for the properties below, and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff loses all its properties except its Quarterstaff bonus and becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-friendship\">Animal Friendship</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-awaken\">Awaken</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-barkskin\">Barkskin</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-locate-animals-or-plants\">Locate Animals or Plants</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-pass-without-trace\">Pass without Trace</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-animals\">Speak with Animals</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-speak-with-plants\">Speak with Plants</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-thorns\">Wall of Thorns</a> (6 charges).</p><p><strong>Tree Form.</strong> You can take an action, plant one end of the staff in fertile earth, and expend 1 charge to transform the staff into a healthy tree 60 feet tall with a 5-foot-diameter trunk and a 20-foot-radius canopy of branches and leaves. The tree looks ordinary but radiates a faint aura of Transmutation magic if targeted by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>. While touching the tree and using another action to speak its command word, you return the staff to its normal form; any creature in the tree falls when it reverts to a staff.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you have a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls. The staff has 10 charges for the properties below, and regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff loses all its properties except its Quarterstaff bonus and becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: Animal Friendship (1 charge), Awaken (5 charges), Barkskin (2 charges), Locate Animals or Plants (2 charges), Speak with Animals (1 charge), Speak with Plants (3 charges), or Wall of Thorns (6 charges). You can also take an action to cast Pass without Trace from the staff at no charge cost.</p><p><strong>Tree Form.</strong> You can take an action, plant one end of the staff in fertile earth, and expend 1 charge to transform the staff into a healthy tree 60 feet tall with a 5-foot-diameter trunk and a 20-foot-radius canopy of branches and leaves. The tree looks ordinary but radiates a faint aura of Transmutation magic if targeted by Detect Magic. While touching the tree and using another action to speak its command word, you return the staff to its normal form; any creature in the tree falls when it reverts to a staff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-withering", "title": "Staff of Withering", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. It can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff; on a hit, it deals damage as a normal Quarterstaff, and you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> to the target and force it to make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a failed save, the target has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> for 1 hour on any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> or saving throw that uses Strength or Constitution.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Warlock)</p><p>This staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. It can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff; on a hit, it deals damage as a normal Quarterstaff, and you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic damage to the target and force it to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage for 1 hour on any ability check or saving throw that uses Strength or Constitution.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-fire", "title": "Staff of Fire", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Fire <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while you hold this staff. The staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-burning-hands\">Burning Hands</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (3 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (4 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff blackens, crumbles into cinders, and is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-frost", "title": "Staff of Frost", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Cold <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> while you hold this staff. The staff has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cone-of-cold\">Cone of Cold</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fog-cloud\">Fog Cloud</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ice-storm\">Ice Storm</a> (4 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-ice\">Wall of Ice</a> (4 charges). The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff turns to water and is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-power", "title": "Staff of Power", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a>, and spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 20 charges for the properties below. It regains 2d8+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff keeps its +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls but loses all other properties (including its remaining Retributive Strike). On a 20, the staff regains 1d8+2 charges.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spell attack bonus: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-cone-of-cold\">Cone of Cold</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (5th-level version, 5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-globe-of-invulnerability\">Globe of Invulnerability</a> (6 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-hold-monster\">Hold Monster</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (5th-level version, 5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> (1 charge), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ray-of-enfeeblement\">Ray of Enfeeblement</a> (1 charge), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-force\">Wall of Force</a> (5 charges).</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class, saving throws, and spell attack rolls. The staff has 20 charges for the properties below. It regains 2d8+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff keeps its +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls but loses all other properties (including its remaining Retributive Strike and Power Strike). On a 20, the staff regains 1d8+2 charges.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an action and expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spell attack bonus: Cone of Cold (5 charges), Fireball (5th-level version, 5 charges), Globe of Invulnerability (6 charges), Hold Monster (5 charges), Levitate (2 charges), Lightning Bolt (5th-level version, 5 charges), Magic Missile (1 charge), Ray of Enfeeblement (1 charge), or Wall of Force (5 charges).</p><p><strong>Power Strike.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target.</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-striking", "title": "Staff of Striking", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. The staff has 10 charges. When you hit with a melee attack using it, you can expend up to 3 of its charges; for each charge expended, the target takes an extra 1d6 Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>. The staff regains 1d6+4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-staff-of-thunder-and-lightning", "title": "Staff of Thunder and Lightning", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. It also has the following properties. Once a property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Lightning.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause the target to take an extra 2d6 Lightning <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a>.</p><p><strong>Thunder.</strong> When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause it to issue a crack of thunder, audible out to 300 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-stunned\">Stunned</a> until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Lightning Strike.</strong> You can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to send a bolt of lightning leaping from the staff's tip in a line 5 feet wide and 120 feet long. Each creature in the line must make a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 9d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a success.</p><p><strong>Thunderclap.</strong> You can take an action to make the staff issue a deafening thunderclap, audible out to 600 feet. Each creature within 60 feet of you, other than you, must make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 2d6 Thunder damage and becoming <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> for 1 minute on a failed save, or taking half as much damage and remaining undeafened on a success.</p><p><strong>Thunder and Lightning.</strong> You can take an action to use the Lightning Strike and Thunderclap properties at the same time. Doing so uses only this combined property's daily use, not those of the two individual properties.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-staves-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-staff-of-the-magi", "title": "Staff of the Magi", "html": "<p><strong>Staff, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)</p><p>This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While you hold it, you gain a +2 bonus to spell <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a>. The staff has 50 charges for the properties below, and regains 4d6+2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll a d20; on a 20, the staff regains 1d12+1 charges.</p><p><strong>Spell Absorption.</strong> While holding the staff, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on saving throws against spells. You can also use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> when another creature casts a spell that targets only you: if you do, the staff absorbs the magic of the spell, canceling its effect and gaining a number of charges equal to the absorbed spell's level. If this brings the staff's total charges above 50, the staff instead immediately triggers its Retributive Strike, as if you had activated it yourself.</p><p><strong>Spells.</strong> While holding the staff, you can take an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> and expend some of its charges to cast one of the following spells from it, using your spell save DC and spellcasting ability: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a> (7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> (3 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-fireball\">Fireball</a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-flaming-sphere\">Flaming Sphere</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-ice-storm\">Ice Storm</a> (4 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-invisibility\">Invisibility</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a> (2 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lightning-bolt\">Lightning Bolt</a> (7th-level version, 7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-passwall\">Passwall</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-plane-shift\">Plane Shift</a> (7 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-telekinesis\">Telekinesis</a> (5 charges), <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wall-of-fire\">Wall of Fire</a> (4 charges), or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (2 charges). You can also take an action to cast, at no charge cost, one of the following spells from it: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-arcane-lock\">Arcane Lock</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-magic\">Detect Magic</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-enlarge-reduce\">Enlarge/Reduce</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-light\">Light</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-mage-hand\">Mage Hand</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-protection-from-evil-and-good\">Protection from Evil and Good</a>.</p><p><strong>Retributive Strike.</strong> You can take an action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface, releasing all its remaining magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on it. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion; if you fail to avoid it, you take Force <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. The staff is destroyed. Every other creature in the area of the explosion must make a DC 17 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 8 times the number of charges within 10 feet of the staff, 6 times the number of charges between 11 and 20 feet, or 4 times the number of charges between 21 and 30 feet, or taking half as much damage on a success.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-scrolls", "title": "Scrolls", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-spell-scroll", "title": "Spell Scroll", "html": "<p><strong>Scroll, Rarity Varies</strong></p><p>A Spell Scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing Material components; otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell this way takes the spell's normal casting time, and once the spell is cast, the scroll crumbles to dust — if the casting is interrupted, the scroll isn't lost.</p><p>If the spell is on your spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast it successfully. The DC equals 10 + the spell's level; on a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect.</p><p>The level of the spell held on the scroll sets its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DC</a>, its attack bonus, and the scroll's own rarity, as shown below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Rarity</th><th>Save DC</th><th>Attack Bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1st</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Legendary</td><td>19</td><td>+11</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Copying a Scroll into a Spellbook.</strong> A Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll can be copied into a spellbook just as other spells can. The copier must succeed on an Intelligence (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-arcana\">Arcana</a>) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level; on a success, the spell is copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the Spell Scroll is destroyed.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Scroll, Rarity Varies</strong></p><p>A Spell Scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's spell list, you can use an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any of the spell's components; otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade and it crumbles to dust — if the casting is interrupted, the scroll isn't lost.</p><p>If the spell is on your class's spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you must make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-ability-check\">ability check</a> using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast it successfully. The DC equals 10 + the spell's level; on a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect.</p><p>The level of the spell held on the scroll sets its <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficulty-class\">saving throw DC</a>, its attack bonus, and the scroll's own rarity, as shown below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Spell Level</th><th>Rarity</th><th>Save DC</th><th>Attack Bonus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1st</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2nd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3rd</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>4th</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5th</td><td>Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8th</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>9th</td><td>Legendary</td><td>19</td><td>+11</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Copying a Scroll into a Spellbook.</strong> A Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll can be copied just as spells in spellbooks can be copied. The copier must succeed on an Intelligence (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-arcana\">Arcana</a>) check with a DC equal to 10 + the spell's level; on a success, the spell is copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the Spell Scroll is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-scroll-of-protection", "title": "Scroll of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Scroll, Rare</strong></p><p>Each Scroll of Protection works against creatures of a specific type, chosen by the DM or determined by rolling on the table below.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Creature Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–10</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a></td></tr><tr><td>11–15</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a></td></tr><tr><td>16–20</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a></td></tr><tr><td>21–25</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Constructs</a></td></tr><tr><td>26–35</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a></td></tr><tr><td>36–45</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a></td></tr><tr><td>46–50</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-humanoid\">Humanoids</a></td></tr><tr><td>51–60</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a></td></tr><tr><td>61–70</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a></td></tr><tr><td>71–75</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giants</a></td></tr><tr><td>76–80</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-monstrosity\">Monstrosities</a></td></tr><tr><td>81–85</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-ooze\">Oozes</a></td></tr><tr><td>86–90</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a></td></tr><tr><td>91–00</td><td><a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Using a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to read the scroll creates a 5-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you. For 5 minutes, creatures of the specified type can't enter or affect anything in the area; however, if you move so that a creature of the specified type would end up inside the area, the effect ends.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, a creature within 5 feet of the Emanation can attempt to overcome it, forcing it to make a DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-charisma\">Charisma</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. On a success, the creature ceases to be affected by the Emanation.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Scroll, Rare</strong></p><p>Each Scroll of Protection works against creatures of one of eight types, chosen by the DM or determined at random: <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-aberration\">Aberrations</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-beast\">Beasts</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-celestial\">Celestials</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-elemental\">Elementals</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fey\">Fey</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiends</a>, <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-plant\">Plants</a>, or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a>.</p><p>Using an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to read the scroll encloses you in an invisible barrier that extends from you to form a 5-foot-radius, 10-foot-high cylinder. For 5 minutes, this barrier prevents creatures of the specified type from entering or affecting anything within it; the cylinder moves with you and remains centered on you, but if you move in such a way that a creature of the specified type would end up inside it, the effect ends.</p><p>A creature can attempt to overcome the barrier by using an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-action\">action</a> to make a DC 15 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-charisma\">Charisma</a> check. On a success, the creature ceases to be affected by the barrier.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor", "title": "Armor", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-armor-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-of-gleaming", "title": "Armor of Gleaming", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>This armor never gets dirty.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-cast-off-armor", "title": "Cast-Off Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>You can doff this armor as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-of-expression", "title": "Shield of Expression", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Common</strong></p><p>The front of this Shield is shaped like a face. While bearing the Shield, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to change the face's expression.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-smoldering-armor", "title": "Smoldering Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Common</strong></p><p>Wisps of harmless, odorless smoke rise from this armor while it is worn.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-adamantine-armor", "title": "Adamantine Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon</strong></p><p>This armor is reinforced with adamantine, one of the hardest substances in existence. While you wear it, any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-critical-hit\">Critical Hit</a> against you becomes a normal hit.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mariner-s-armor", "title": "Mariner's Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-swim-speed\">Swim Speed</a> equal to your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-speed\">Speed</a>. In addition, if you start your turn underwater with 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>, you immediately regain 1d4 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. The armor can't heal anyone again until the next dawn.</p><p>The armor is decorated with fish and shell motifs.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mithral-armor", "title": "Mithral Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon</strong></p><p>Mithral is a light, flexible metal, and armor made from it can be worn under normal clothes. If the armor normally imposes <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on Dexterity (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-stealth\">Stealth</a>) checks or has a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> requirement, the mithral version of the armor doesn't.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sentinel-shield", "title": "Sentinel Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-initiative\">Initiative</a> rolls and Wisdom (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-perception\">Perception</a>) checks. The Shield is emblazoned with a symbol of an eye.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-1", "title": "Shield, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Uncommon</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-1", "title": "Armor, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-resistance", "title": "Armor of Resistance", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one type of damage while you wear this armor. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d10</th><th>Damage Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Force</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Necrotic</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Psychic</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Thunder</td></tr></tbody></table>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-vulnerability", "title": "Armor of Vulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this armor, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one of the following damage types: Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing. The DM chooses the type or determines it randomly.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-vulnerability\">Vulnerability</a> to the other two of the three damage types associated with the armor (not the one to which it grants Resistance).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-arrow-catching-shield", "title": "Arrow-Catching Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> against ranged <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> while you wield this Shield. This bonus is in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p><p>Whenever an attacker makes a ranged attack roll against a target within 5 feet of you, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to become the target of the attack instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-elven-chain", "title": "Elven Chain", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a> while you wear this armor. You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Chain Shirt), Rare</strong></p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to AC while you wear this armor. You are considered proficient with this armor even if you lack proficiency with medium armor.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-glamoured-studded-leather", "title": "Glamoured Studded Leather", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Studded Leather Armor), Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. You can also take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor. You decide what it looks like, including color, style, and accessories, but the armor retains its normal bulk and weight. The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or doff the armor.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-2", "title": "Shield, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-of-missile-attraction", "title": "Shield of Missile Attraction", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage\">damage</a> from attacks made with Ranged weapons.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> This Shield is cursed. Attuning to it curses you until you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic. Removing the Shield fails to end the curse on you. Whenever an attack with a Ranged weapon targets a creature within 10 feet of you, the curse causes you to become the target instead.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-animated-shield", "title": "Animated Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you can speak its command word as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animated for 1 minute, until you use a Bonus Action to end this effect, or until you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition or die, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-2", "title": "Armor, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-demon-armor", "title": "Demon Armor", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, and you know Abyssal. In addition, the armor's clawed gauntlets allow your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-unarmed-strike\">Unarmed Strikes</a> to deal 1d8 Slashing damage instead of the usual Bludgeoning damage, and you gain a +1 bonus to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> of your Unarmed Strikes.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> Once you don this cursed armor, you can't doff it unless you are targeted by a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-remove-curse\">Remove Curse</a> spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> on attack rolls against demons and on saving throws against their spells and special abilities.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dragon-scale-mail", "title": "Dragon Scale Mail", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against the breath weapons of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragons</a>, and you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to one damage type determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the table).</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Dragon</th><th>Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Additionally, you can focus your senses as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of you that is of the same type as the armor. This action can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Dragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to one damage type determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the table).</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Dragon</th><th>Resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Additionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of you that is of the same type as the armor. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dwarven-plate", "title": "Dwarven Plate", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Half Plate Armor or Plate Armor), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>. In addition, if an effect moves you against your will along the ground, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to reduce the distance you are moved by up to 10 feet.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Plate), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you gain a +2 bonus to AC. In addition, if an effect moves you against your will along the ground, you can use your reaction to reduce the distance you are moved by up to 10 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-shield-3", "title": "Shield, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong></p><p>While holding this Shield, you have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>, in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-spellguard-shield", "title": "Spellguard Shield", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Shield), Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While holding this Shield, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells and other magical effects, and spell attack rolls have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-disadvantage\">Disadvantage</a> against you.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-armor-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-armor-3", "title": "Armor, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Legendary</strong></p><p>While wearing this armor, you have a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-armor-class\">Armor Class</a>.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-armor-of-invulnerability", "title": "Armor of Invulnerability", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">Resistance</a> to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while you wear this armor.</p><p><strong>Metal Shell.</strong> You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to give yourself <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-immunity\">Immunity</a> to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><h5>Legacy Version (2014)</h5><p><strong>Armor (Plate), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You have resistance to nonmagical damage while you wear this armor. Additionally, you can use an action to make yourself immune to nonmagical damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this special action is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-plate-armor-of-etherealness", "title": "Plate Armor of Etherealness", "html": "<p><strong>Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you're wearing this armor, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a command word to gain the effect of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-etherealness\">Etherealness</a> spell. The spell ends immediately if you remove the armor or take a Magic action to repeat the command word. This property of the armor can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons", "title": "Weapons", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-weapons-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-moon-touched-sword", "title": "Moon-Touched Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Common</strong></p>\n<p>This blade glows with a faint silvery light, shedding dim light in a 5-foot radius.\nWhenever you hit an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> creature with it, that target takes an extra 1d4 Radiant damage.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-javelin-of-lightning", "title": "Javelin of Lightning", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Javelin), Uncommon</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic javelin.\nWhen you throw it, you can speak its command word, causing it to transform in flight into a bolt of lightning that streaks to its original target and beyond, forming a line 5 feet wide and 120 feet long.\nEach creature in that line other than you must make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dexterity\">Dexterity</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 13), taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much on a success.\nThe javelin is destroyed once it deals this damage, but its lightning-scarred remains can be used to craft a new javelin of lightning.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-vengeance", "title": "Sword of Vengeance", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Uncommon</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. This weapon is cursed and possessed by a vengeful spirit, though the curse remains hidden until you attune to it. Becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you: you become unwilling to part with the sword, keeping it on your person at all times, and you have disadvantage on attack rolls made with any other weapon.\nWhenever you take damage from another creature in combat, you must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or fly into a vengeful compulsion, attacking the creature that damaged you on your turns until either it or you drops to 0 Hit Points, or until you can't reach that creature to make a melee attack against it.\nThe curse can be broken in the usual ways. Casting Banishment on the sword also forces the vengeful spirit out of it, after which the sword becomes a +1 weapon with no other properties.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-trident-of-fish-command", "title": "Trident of Fish Command", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Trident), Uncommon</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). It has 3 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge and use an action to cast the Dominate Beast spell (save DC 15) from it,\nbut the target must be a beast that has an innate swimming Speed. The trident regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-of-warning", "title": "Weapon of Warning", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any), Uncommon</strong></p>\n<p>This magic weapon (requires attunement) warns you of danger. While it's on your person, you have advantage on Initiative rolls.\nIn addition, you and any of your companions within 30 feet of you can't be surprised while the weapon is on your person, except when Incapacitated by something other than nonmagical sleep.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-1", "title": "Weapon, +1", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any), Uncommon</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-berserker-axe", "title": "Berserker Axe", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Battleaxe, Greataxe, or Halberd), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). While attuned to it, your Hit Point maximum also increases by 1 for each level you have attained.\nThis weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you're unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it within reach at all times, and you have disadvantage on attack rolls with any weapon other than this one.\nWhenever another creature damages you while the weapon is in your possession, you must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or go berserk: you regard the creature nearest to you that you can see or hear as your enemy (chosen at random if more than one is equally near), and on each of your turns you must move as close to that creature as possible and take the Attack action against it. This berserk state ends when you start a turn with no creature within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version</h5>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon (any axe, requires attunement). While attuned to it, your hit point maximum also increases by 1 for each level you have attained.\nThis weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you're unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it within reach at all times, and you have disadvantage on attack rolls with any weapon other than this one, unless no foe you can see or hear is within 60 feet of you.\nWhenever a hostile creature damages you while the weapon is in your possession, you must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or go berserk. While berserk, on each of your turns you must use your action to attack the creature nearest to you with the weapon; if you can make extra attacks as part of that action, you use them, moving to attack the next-nearest creature once your current target is felled. This berserk state ends when you start a turn with no creature within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dagger-of-venom", "title": "Dagger of Venom", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Dagger), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. You can use an action to cause thick, black poison to coat its blade, which lasts until an attack with this weapon hits a creature or 1 minute passes, whichever comes first.\nOn a hit while coated, the target must succeed on a Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or take an extra 2d10 Poison damage and become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-poisoned\">Poisoned</a> for 1 minute. The dagger can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dragon-slayer", "title": "Dragon Slayer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any bladed weapon), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> with it, the target takes an extra 3d6 damage of the weapon's type.\nWhile you hold this weapon, you have advantage on <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of Dragons.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-flame-tongue", "title": "Flame Tongue", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any bladed weapon), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). You can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a> to speak this weapon's command word, causing flames to erupt from it.\nThese flames emit bright light in a 40-foot radius and dim light for an additional 40 feet, and they don't harm you or the weapon. While the weapon is ablaze, it deals an extra 2d6 Fire damage to any target it hits.\nThe flames last until you use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a> to speak the command word again, until you drop or sheathe the weapon, or until you die. Immersing the weapon in water extinguishes the flames early.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-giant-slayer", "title": "Giant Slayer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any bladed weapon), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon. When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> with it, the target takes an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon's type.\nIn addition, when a Giant within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to force that creature to make a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15), knocking it <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> on a failure.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-disruption", "title": "Mace of Disruption", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic mace (requires attunement). When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that creature takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage.\nThat target must also succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> of you for 1 minute. If you roll a natural 20 on the attack roll against a Fiend or Undead, that creature is instead destroyed if it fails a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15).</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-smiting", "title": "Mace of Smiting", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic mace. This bonus increases to +3 when you use the mace to attack a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-construct\">Construct</a>. When you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 Bludgeoning damage, or an extra 14 Bludgeoning damage if it's a Construct. If a Construct has 25 Hit Points or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-mace-of-terror", "title": "Mace of Terror", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Mace), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic mace (requires attunement). It has 3 charges. While holding it, you can use an action and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror.\nEach creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or become <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-frightened\">Frightened</a> of you for 1 minute. A frightened creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The mace regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sun-blade", "title": "Sun Blade", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longsword), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>This item appears to be a longsword hilt. While grasping it, you can use a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a> to cause a blade of pure, crackling radiance to spring into existence, or make the blade disappear.\nWhile the blade exists, this magic weapon (requires attunement) has the finesse property, and you gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with it. On a hit, the target takes Radiant damage instead of the weapon's normal damage type.\nThe blade emits bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 15 feet; this light can be extinguished as part of dismissing the blade. When you hit an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that target takes an extra 1d8 Radiant damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-life-stealing", "title": "Sword of Life Stealing", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). When you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 3d6 Necrotic damage, and you regain Hit Points equal to that necrotic damage dealt.\nA construct or undead target is unaffected by this extra necrotic damage.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-wounding", "title": "Sword of Wounding", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). On a hit, the target takes an extra 2d6 Necrotic damage and begins bleeding magically. At the start of each of its turns, the bleeding target takes 1d6 Necrotic damage.\nAny creature can take an action to stanch the wound with a successful <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-wisdom\">Wisdom</a> (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-medicine\">Medicine</a>) check (DC 15), and the bleeding also ends if the target receives magical healing.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vicious-weapon", "title": "Vicious Weapon", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>When you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 7 damage of the weapon's type.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-2", "title": "Weapon, +2", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any), Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-dancing-sword", "title": "Dancing Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a> to toss this magic weapon (requires attunement) into the air. When you do so, the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself, using your own <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> and adding your ability modifier to the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage roll</a>.\nWhile the weapon hovers, you can use a bonus action to cause it to fly up to 30 feet to another spot within 30 feet of you, and as part of that same bonus action you can cause it to attack a creature within 5 feet of it again. After the hovering weapon has attacked four times, it flies up to 30 feet and tries to return to your hand; if you have no hand free, or if it has no unobstructed path to you, it falls to the ground instead.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-dwarven-thrower", "title": "Dwarven Thrower", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Warhammer), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic warhammer (requires attunement). It counts as a thrown weapon with a normal and long range of 20/60 feet, and returns to your hand immediately after it's thrown and hits or misses.\nWhen you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> with a thrown attack using it, that target takes an extra 1d8 damage, and the bonus to attack and damage rolls with the hammer increases to +3 against Giants only.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-frost-brand", "title": "Frost Brand", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>When you hit with an attack using this magic sword (requires attunement), the target takes an extra 1d6 Cold damage. While you hold it, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">resistance</a> to Fire damage.\nIn freezing temperatures, the blade sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. When you draw this weapon, you can extinguish all nonmagical flames within 30 feet of you; this property can be used no more than once per hour.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-nine-lives-stealer", "title": "Nine Lives Stealer", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). The sword has 9 charges. If you hit a creature that has 100 Hit Points or fewer with it, that creature must succeed on a Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or be slain instantly as the sword tears its life force from its body, and the sword loses 1 charge.\nIf the sword has no charges left when this happens, it doesn't steal the creature's life. Once the sword has stolen 9 lives, it can't do so again for 1d4 days as the swirling life energies within it settle.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-oathbow", "title": "Oathbow", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longbow), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>This magic bow (requires attunement) whispers in Elvish when you nock an arrow to it, \"Swift defeat to my enemies.\" When you use an action to speak the phrase \"Farewell, &lt;name&gt;,\" naming a creature you can see within range, you designate that creature as your sworn enemy until it dies or until you use this property again.\nWhen you make a ranged attack roll with this weapon against your sworn enemy, you have advantage on the roll. Your target also gains no benefit from cover other than total cover, and you suffer no disadvantage from attacking at long range against it. If the attack hits, your sworn enemy takes an extra 3d6 Piercing damage.\nWhile your sworn enemy lives, you have disadvantage on attack rolls with all other weapons. If your sworn enemy dies, you can choose a new one after a day has passed. A creature can only be designated as the sworn enemy of one oathbow at a time.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-scimitar-of-speed", "title": "Scimitar of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Scimitar), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). You can also make one attack with it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">bonus action</a> on each of your turns.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-sharpness", "title": "Sword of Sharpness", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>This magic weapon (requires attunement) deals maximum damage against an object it hits. When you attack a creature with it and roll a 20 on the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">d20 for the attack roll</a>, that target takes an extra 14 Slashing damage and gains one level of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-exhaustion\">Exhaustion</a>.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version</h5>\n<p>This magic weapon (any sword that deals slashing damage, requires attunement) deals maximum damage against an object it hits. When you attack a creature with it and roll a 20 on the attack roll, that target takes an extra 4d6 Slashing damage. You then roll another d20: on a 20, you lop off one of the target's limbs (with the effect of that loss determined by the DM), or a portion of its body if it has no limb to sever.\nYou can also speak the sword's command word to make the blade shed bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. Speaking the command word again, or sheathing the sword, puts the light out.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-weapon-3", "title": "Weapon, +3", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any), Very Rare</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-defender", "title": "Defender", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any bladed weapon), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). At the start of each of your turns, you can divide this +3 bonus between the weapon's attack and damage rolls and your Armor Class, assigning a portion of the bonus to each in whole numbers as you choose.\nThis distribution lasts until the start of your next turn, when you can change it again. If you aren't proficient with the weapon, you can still gain this benefit as long as you are holding it.\nThis weapon can telepathically communicate with you when you are within 120 feet of it, and it has hearing and darkvision out to 120 feet, letting it act as your eyes and ears in some circumstances.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-hammer-of-thunderbolts", "title": "Hammer of Thunderbolts", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Warhammer), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic warhammer (requires attunement). While attuned to it, you also gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls made with thrown weapons.\nThe hammer counts as a thrown weapon with a normal and long range of 20/60 feet, and returns to your hand immediately after it's thrown and hits or misses.\nIf you are also wearing a belt and gauntlets of matching giant strength while attuned to the hammer, its bonus to attack and damage rolls rises to +3, and the following additional properties become active. When you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> with it, the target takes an extra 2d10 Thunder damage and must succeed on a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> (DC 15) or be knocked <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> and Stunned until the end of its next turn.\nAgainst a target that isn't a Giant, this attack instead deals an extra 1d8 Thunder damage, and thunder booms audibly out to 300 feet.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-holy-avenger", "title": "Holy Avenger", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any bladed weapon), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement by a creature that channels divine power to smite its foes).\nWhen you hit a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-fiend\">Fiend</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-undead\">Undead</a> with it, that target takes an extra 2d10 Radiant damage. While you hold this weapon, you and friendly creatures within 10 feet of you have a +2 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throws</a> against spells and other magical effects.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-luck-blade", "title": "Luck Blade", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic sword (requires attunement). While attuned to it, you also gain a +1 bonus to any saving throw you make to avoid or end an effect, usable whenever an effect you dislike would otherwise take hold; using this property doesn't require an action.\nThe sword has 1d4-1 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell from it. This property can't be used again until the next dawn; if the sword has no charges remaining, it can never be used this way again.</p>\n<h5>Legacy Version</h5>\n<p>You gain a +1 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic sword (requires attunement). This is one of the few sentient weapons in the multiverse that isn't tied to a single weapon type — it can take the form of a Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, Sickle, or Shortsword.\nWhile attuned to it, you also have a Luck property: once per turn, when you fail a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-d20-test\">D20 Test</a>, you can reroll it, and you must use the new roll.\nThe sword has 1d3 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 of its charges to cast the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell from it. The sword regains 1 expended charge daily at dawn, but once its charges reach 0, roll a d20: on a 1, the sword's magic is permanently destroyed.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-answering", "title": "Sword of Answering", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Shortsword), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic shortsword (requires attunement). This weapon is sentient and has its own goals and agenda, wanting most of all to be reunited with its paired blade, a Sword of Answering carried by another creature somewhere in the world.\nThe sword can communicate telepathically with you while you're holding it, and its purpose is to seek out and destroy those who threaten justice and order. Once per turn, when a creature within 5 feet of you damages you, you can use your <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-reaction\">Reaction</a> to make a melee attack with this sword against that creature.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-vorpal-sword", "title": "Vorpal Sword", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (any sword that deals slashing damage), Legendary</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic weapon (requires attunement). In addition, the weapon ignores resistance to Slashing damage.\nWhen you attack a creature that has at least one head with this weapon and roll a 20 on the attack roll, you cut off one of the creature's heads. The creature dies if it can't survive without the lost head. A creature is immune to this effect if it's immune to Slashing damage, doesn't have or need a head, has legendary actions, or the DM decides it's too big for its head to be cut off with this weapon; such a creature instead takes an extra 6d8 Slashing damage from the hit.</p>"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-weapons-artifact", "title": "Artifact", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-axe-of-the-dwarvish-lords", "title": "Axe of the Dwarvish Lords", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Battleaxe), Artifact</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic battleaxe (requires attunement). While attuned to it, you have Darkvision out to 120 feet, and you have advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks made to follow tracks and on checks made to detect the presence of secret doors.\nThe axe deals an extra 3d6 damage against any <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-giant\">Giant</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"creature-type-dragon\">Dragon</a> it hits, and while you hold it, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-resistance\">resistance</a> to damage from any Dragon's breath weapon.\nOnce per dawn, you can also cast the Stone Shape or Transmute Rock spell from the axe without a spell slot. As a legendary artifact, the axe carries a random minor and major property of the DM's choosing, and a special purpose that can trigger a growing curse in a wielder who strays from it.</p>"}, {"id": "magic-item-sword-of-kas", "title": "Sword of Kas", "html": "<p><strong>Weapon (Longsword), Artifact</strong></p>\n<p>You gain a +3 bonus to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack rolls</a> and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-damage-roll\">damage rolls</a> made with this magic longsword (requires attunement). This sentient blade deals an extra 3d6 Necrotic damage on a hit, and once per turn when you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points with it, you regain Hit Points equal to the weapon's Necrotic damage dealt.\nWhile attuned to it, you can also use an action to cast the Fear spell (save DC 18) from the sword once per dawn. The sword seeks to sever the hand of any creature that opposes its wielder or, failing that, to be reunited with the severed hand of the lich Kas, and it resists any attempt to be destroyed or given away by a wielder it disfavors.\nAs a legendary artifact, the sword carries additional random minor and major properties of the DM's choosing.</p>"}]}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items", "title": "Wondrous Items", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-common", "title": "Common", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-bead-of-nourishment", "title": "Bead of Nourishment", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This flavorless, gelatinous bead dissolves on your tongue and gives you as much nourishment as one day of Rations.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bead-of-refreshment", "title": "Bead of Refreshment", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This flavorless, gelatinous bead dissolves in a liquid, turning up to a pint of it into fresh, cold drinking water. It has no effect on magical liquids or on harmful substances such as poison.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-false-tracks", "title": "Boots of False Tracks", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can make them leave tracks matching those of any kind of Humanoid of your size.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-candle-of-the-deep", "title": "Candle of the Deep", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This candle's flame isn't extinguished when the candle is immersed in water. It gives off light and heat like an ordinary candle.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-charlatan-s-die", "title": "Charlatan's Die", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Whenever you roll this six-sided die, you can choose which number it shows.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-billowing", "title": "Cloak of Billowing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to make it billow dramatically for 1 minute.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-many-fashions", "title": "Cloak of Many Fashions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to change the garment's style, color, and apparent quality. Its weight doesn't change. Whatever it looks like, it can only ever be a cloak; it can copy the look of other magic cloaks but doesn't gain their magical properties.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-clockwork-amulet", "title": "Clockwork Amulet", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This copper amulet holds tiny interlocking gears and is powered by magic from Mechanus, the plane of clockwork predictability; faint ticking and whirring comes from inside it. When you make an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-attack-roll\">attack roll</a> while wearing it, you can skip rolling the d20 and treat the die as showing a 10. Once you use this property, you can't use it again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-clothes-of-mending", "title": "Clothes of Mending", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This elegant outfit mends itself to counteract daily wear and tear. Pieces of the outfit that are destroyed can't be repaired this way.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dark-shard-amulet", "title": "Dark Shard Amulet", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Warlock)</p><p>This amulet is made from a shard of resilient material that comes from an otherworldly realm. While you wear it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use the amulet as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Warlock spells.</p><p><strong>Unknown Spell.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can try to cast a cantrip you don't know. The cantrip must be on the Warlock spell list and have a casting time of an action, and you make a DC 10 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you cast the spell. On a failure, the spell fails and the action used to cast it is wasted. Either way, you can't use this property again until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dread-helm", "title": "Dread Helm", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you wear this fearsome steel helm, your eyes glow red and the rest of your face is hidden in shadow.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ear-horn-of-hearing", "title": "Ear Horn of Hearing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you hold this horn up to your ear, it suppresses the effects of the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-deafened\">Deafened</a> condition on you.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-enduring-spellbook", "title": "Enduring Spellbook", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This spellbook, and anything written in it, can't be damaged by fire or water. It also doesn't deteriorate with age.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ersatz-eye", "title": "Ersatz Eye", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This magical eye replaces one that was lost or removed. While it sits in your eye socket, you can see through the tiny orb as though it were your natural eye. You can insert or remove it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and it can't be removed against your will while you are alive.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-vermin", "title": "Hat of Vermin", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This hat has 3 charges. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to summon your choice of a Bat, a Frog, or a Rat. The creature appears in the hat and tries to get away from you as fast as it can. It is Indifferent toward you and everyone else, isn't under your control, behaves like an ordinary creature of its kind, and disappears after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-hit-points\">Hit Points</a>. The hat regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-hat-of-wizardry", "title": "Hat of Wizardry", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Wizard)</p><p>This cone-shaped hat is decorated with moons and stars. While you wear it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting Focus.</strong> You can use the hat as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your Wizard spells.</p><p><strong>Unknown Spell.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can try to cast a cantrip you don't know. The cantrip must be on the Wizard spell list and have a casting time of an action, and you make a DC 10 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a success, you cast the spell. On a failure, the spell fails and the action used to cast it is wasted. Either way, you can't use this property again until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-heward-s-handy-spice-pouch", "title": "Heward's Handy Spice Pouch", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This belt pouch looks empty and has 10 charges. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to name any nonmagical food seasoning (salt, pepper, saffron, cilantro, and so on) and pull a pinch of it from the pouch; a pinch is enough to season one meal. The pouch regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-horn-of-silent-alarm", "title": "Horn of Silent Alarm", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This horn has 4 charges and regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can blow the horn and expend 1 charge. One creature of your choice within 600 feet of the horn hears its blare; no one else does.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-illusions", "title": "Instrument of Illusions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While you play this musical instrument, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to create harmless, illusory visual effects in a 5-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from the instrument. If you are a Bard, the Emanation is 15 feet instead. Sample effects include luminous musical notes, a spectral dancer, butterflies, and gently falling snow. The effects have no substance or sound and are obviously illusory. They end when you stop playing.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-instrument-of-scribing", "title": "Instrument of Scribing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This musical instrument has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. While you play it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and expend 1 charge to write a magical message on a nonmagical object or surface you can see within 30 feet of you. The message can be up to six words long and is written in a language you know. If you are a Bard, you can scribe an additional seven words and make the message glow faintly, so it can be read even in nonmagical <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a>. Casting <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> on the message erases it; otherwise it fades after 24 hours.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-lock-of-trickery", "title": "Lock of Trickery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This lock looks like an ordinary lock (the kind described in the Player's Handbook) and comes with a single key. Its tumblers magically shift to thwart burglars, so Dexterity checks made to pick it have Disadvantage.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-mystery-key", "title": "Mystery Key", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>A question mark is worked into the head of this key. The key has a 5 percent chance of unlocking any lock it is inserted into. Once it unlocks something, the key disappears.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-orb-of-direction", "title": "Orb of Direction", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>You can use this orb as an Arcane Focus. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to learn which way is magnetic north. Nothing happens if you use it somewhere that has no magnetic north.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-orb-of-time", "title": "Orb of Time", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>You can use this orb as an Arcane Focus. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to learn whether it is morning, afternoon, evening, or nighttime. This works only on the Material Plane.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-perfume-of-bewitching-wondrous", "title": "Perfume of Bewitching", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This tiny vial holds enough magic perfume for one use. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to apply it to yourself, and its effect lasts 1 hour. For that duration, you have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-advantage\">Advantage</a> on all Charisma (Deception and Persuasion) checks made to influence a creature within 5 feet of you.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pipe-of-smoke-monsters", "title": "Pipe of Smoke Monsters", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>While smoking this pipe, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to exhale a puff of smoke shaped like a creature, such as a dragon, a flumph, or a slaad. The shape must fit within a 1-foot cube and loses its form after a few seconds, becoming an ordinary puff of smoke.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pole-of-angling", "title": "Pole of Angling", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This item works as a Pole. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to turn it into a fishing pole with a hook, line, and reel, or to turn the fishing pole back into a Pole.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pole-of-collapsing", "title": "Pole of Collapsing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This item works as a Pole. While holding it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to collapse it into a 1-foot-long rod for easy storage (its weight doesn't change), or to return the rod to a Pole. The rod lengthens only as far as the surrounding space allows.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-pot-of-awakening", "title": "Pot of Awakening", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>If you plant an ordinary shrub in this 10-pound clay pot and let it grow for 30 days, the shrub magically becomes an Awakened Shrub at the end of that time. When it awakens, its roots break the pot and destroy it. The awakened shrub is Friendly toward you and obeys your commands; without commands from you, it does nothing.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-prosthetic-limb", "title": "Prosthetic Limb", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This magic item replaces a lost limb, such as a hand, arm, foot, leg, or similar body part. While attached, it works exactly like the part it replaces. You can detach or reattach it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, and it can't be removed against your will while you are alive.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rival-coin", "title": "Rival Coin", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This gold coin has a creature embossed on each face. The two must be famous rivals or enemies of each other (for example, Iggwilv on one side and Mordenkainen on the other, or Venger and Tiamat). One figure is on the heads side, the other on the tails side.</p><p>The coin has 1 charge and regains it daily at dawn. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to toss the coin and expend its charge. Roll any die: an even number means heads, an odd number means tails, and the result also decides the effect.</p><p><strong>Heads.</strong> Target one creature you can see within 60 feet. The target makes a DC 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 2d4 Psychic damage and has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and suffers no other effect.</p><p><strong>Tails.</strong> You take 1d4 Psychic damage.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-rope-of-mending", "title": "Rope of Mending", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This 50-foot coil of rope repairs itself when cut into any number of smaller pieces. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can make all pieces that are touching each other and not otherwise in use knit back together. If a section of the rope is lost or destroyed, it is permanently shorter.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-ruby-of-the-war-mage", "title": "Ruby of the War Mage", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement by a Spellcaster)</p><p>Etched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby lets you use a Simple or Martial weapon as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-spellcasting-focus\">Spellcasting Focus</a> for your spells. For this to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing it against the weapon for at least 10 minutes. After that, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, the weapon is destroyed, or your attunement to the ruby ends.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-talking-doll", "title": "Talking Doll", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While this doll is within 5 feet of you, you can spend a Short Rest telling it up to six phrases, none longer than six words, and setting a condition under which it speaks each one. You can also replace old phrases with new ones. Whatever the condition is, it must occur within 5 feet of the doll to make it speak. For example, whenever someone picks the doll up, it might say, \"I want a piece of candy.\" The doll's phrases are lost when your attunement to it ends.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-tankard-of-sobriety", "title": "Tankard of Sobriety", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>This tankard has a stern face sculpted into one side. You can drink ale, wine, or any other nonmagical alcoholic drink poured into it without becoming inebriated. The tankard has no effect on magical liquids or on harmful substances such as poison.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-veteran-s-cane", "title": "Veteran's Cane", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Common</strong></p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, you can turn this walking cane into an ordinary Longsword, or turn the Longsword back into a walking cane. You must be holding the item to do either.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-uncommon", "title": "Uncommon", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-amulet-of-proof-against-detection-and-location", "title": "Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this amulet, you can't be targeted by Divination spells or perceived through magical scrying sensors unless you allow it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-holding", "title": "Bag of Holding", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This bag's interior is far larger than its outside, roughly 2 feet square and 4 feet deep inside. It can hold up to 500 pounds, not exceeding 64 cubic feet, and it weighs 5 pounds regardless of its contents. Retrieving an item from it requires a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>.</p><p>If the bag is overloaded, pierced, or torn, it is destroyed and its contents scatter across the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"plane-astral\">Astral Plane</a>. If it's turned inside out, its contents spill out unharmed, but the bag must be put right before it can be used again. It holds enough air for 10 minutes of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.</p><p>Placing a Bag of Holding inside an extradimensional space created by a Heward's Handy Haversack, a Portable Hole, or a similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a one-way gate to the Astral Plane at that spot. Each creature within a 10-foot-radius <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-sphere\">Sphere</a> centered on the gate is sucked through to a random location on the Astral Plane, and the gate then closes for good.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bag-of-tricks", "title": "Bag of Tricks", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This bag, made of gray, rust, or tan cloth, seems empty, but reaching inside reveals a small, fuzzy object. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can pull the object out and throw it up to 20 feet. When it lands, it becomes a creature determined by rolling on the table matching the bag's color (stat blocks are in the Monster Manual). The creature vanishes at the next dawn or when it drops to 0 Hit Points.</p><p>The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to command how it moves and acts on its next turn; without orders, it acts as befits its nature. Once three fuzzy objects have been pulled from the bag, it can't be used again until the next dawn.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d8</th><th>Gray Bag</th><th>Rust Bag</th><th>Tan Bag</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Weasel</td><td>Rat</td><td>Jackal</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Giant Rat</td><td>Owl</td><td>Ape</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Badger</td><td>Mastiff</td><td>Baboon</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Boar</td><td>Goat</td><td>Axe Beak</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Panther</td><td>Giant Goat</td><td>Black Bear</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Giant Badger</td><td>Giant Boar</td><td>Giant Weasel</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Dire Wolf</td><td>Lion</td><td>Giant Hyena</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Giant Elk</td><td>Brown Bear</td><td>Tiger</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-elvenkind", "title": "Boots of Elvenkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While you wear these boots, your steps make no sound regardless of the surface, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-striding-and-springing", "title": "Boots of Striding and Springing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, your Speed becomes 30 feet unless it's higher, and it isn't reduced by carrying weight over your carrying capacity or by wearing Heavy armor. Once on each of your turns, you can jump up to 30 feet by spending only 10 feet of movement.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-the-winterlands", "title": "Boots of the Winterlands", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These furred boots are snug and warm. While wearing them, you have Resistance to Cold damage and can tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower without extra protection. You also ignore <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a> created by ice or snow.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bracers-of-archery", "title": "Bracers of Archery", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing these bracers, you have proficiency with the Longbow and Shortbow, and you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls made with those weapons.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-brooch-of-shielding", "title": "Brooch of Shielding", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this brooch, you have Resistance to Force damage and Immunity to damage from the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-magic-missile\">Magic Missile</a> spell.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-broom-of-flying", "title": "Broom of Flying", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This wooden broom works like an ordinary one until you stand astride it and take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to make it hover beneath you, at which point you can ride it through the air. It has a Fly Speed of 50 feet and can carry up to 400 pounds, but its Fly Speed drops to 30 feet while carrying more than 200 pounds. It stops hovering when you land or when you're no longer riding it.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile if you name the location and are familiar with it. It returns to you when you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> and use a command word, provided it's still within 1 mile of you.</p><h5>Legacy Version</h5><p>In the 2014 rules the broom doesn't require attunement, and you activate it by speaking its command word rather than taking a Magic action. It weighs 3 pounds. It hovers beneath you when you speak the command word and stand astride it, with a flying speed of 50 feet, and carries up to 400 pounds (30 feet while carrying over 200 pounds). It stops hovering when you land. You can send it to a destination within 1 mile by speaking the command word, naming the location, and being familiar with the place, and it returns when you speak another command word, if it's still within 1 mile.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-circlet-of-blasting", "title": "Circlet of Blasting", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>While wearing this circlet, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scorching-ray\">Scorching Ray</a> with it (+5 to hit). The circlet can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-elvenkind", "title": "Cloak of Elvenkind", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this cloak, Wisdom (Perception) checks made to perceive you have Disadvantage, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-protection", "title": "Cloak of Protection", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws while you wear this cloak.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-the-manta-ray", "title": "Cloak of the Manta Ray", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this cloak, you can breathe underwater and have a Swim Speed of 60 feet.</p><h5>Legacy Version</h5><p>In the 2014 rules the cloak doesn't require attunement. The benefits apply only while the hood is up: you can breathe underwater and have a swimming speed of 60 feet, and pulling the hood up or down takes an action.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-decanter-of-endless-water", "title": "Decanter of Endless Water", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This 2-pound stoppered flask sloshes when shaken as if it holds water. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can remove the stopper and speak one of three command words, and fresh or salt water (your choice) pours out until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Splash.</strong> 1 gallon of water.</p><p><strong>Fountain.</strong> 5 gallons of water.</p><p><strong>Geyser.</strong> 30 gallons of water gush out in a 30-foot-long, 1-foot-wide <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-line\">Line</a>. If you're holding the decanter, you can aim the geyser (no action required). One creature of your choice in the Line must succeed on a DC 13 Strength <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a> or take 1d4 Bludgeoning damage and have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-prone\">Prone</a> condition. Instead of a creature, you can target one unattended object in the Line that weighs no more than 200 pounds; the geyser knocks it over.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-deck-of-illusions", "title": "Deck of Illusions", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This box holds a full deck of 34 cards: 32 depicting specific creatures and 2 with mirrored surfaces. A deck found as treasure is usually missing 1d20 − 1 cards. The magic works only if cards are drawn at random.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can draw a random card and throw it to the ground within 30 feet of you. An illusion of the creature it depicts (see the table) forms over the card and remains until dispelled. It looks and behaves like a real creature of its kind but can do no harm. While you're within 120 feet of it and can see it, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to move it anywhere within 30 feet of its card.</p><p>Any physical interaction reveals the illusion, since objects pass through it. A creature that takes a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-study\">Study action</a> to inspect it recognizes it as an illusion with a successful DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check. The illusion lasts until its card is moved or the illusion is dispelled (<a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dispel-magic\">Dispel Magic</a> or similar). When it ends, the card's image disappears and the card can't be used again.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>1d100</th><th>Illusion</th><th>1d100</th><th>Illusion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>01–03</td><td>Adult Red Dragon</td><td>52–54</td><td>Hobgoblin Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>04–06</td><td>Archmage</td><td>55–57</td><td>Incubus</td></tr><tr><td>07–09</td><td>Assassin</td><td>58–60</td><td>Iron Golem</td></tr><tr><td>10–12</td><td>Bandit Captain</td><td>61–63</td><td>Knight</td></tr><tr><td>13–15</td><td>Beholder</td><td>64–66</td><td>Kobold Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>16–18</td><td>Berserker</td><td>67–69</td><td>Lich</td></tr><tr><td>19–21</td><td>Bugbear Warrior</td><td>70–72</td><td>Medusa</td></tr><tr><td>22–24</td><td>Cloud Giant</td><td>73–75</td><td>Night Hag</td></tr><tr><td>25–27</td><td>Druid</td><td>76–78</td><td>Ogre</td></tr><tr><td>28–30</td><td>Erinyes</td><td>79–81</td><td>Oni</td></tr><tr><td>31–33</td><td>Ettin</td><td>82–84</td><td>Priest</td></tr><tr><td>34–36</td><td>Fire Giant</td><td>85–87</td><td>Succubus</td></tr><tr><td>37–39</td><td>Frost Giant</td><td>88–90</td><td>Troll</td></tr><tr><td>40–42</td><td>Gnoll Warrior</td><td>91–93</td><td>Warrior Veteran</td></tr><tr><td>43–45</td><td>Goblin Warrior</td><td>94–96</td><td>Wyvern</td></tr><tr><td>46–48</td><td>Guardian Naga</td><td>97–00</td><td>The card drawer</td></tr><tr><td>49–51</td><td>Hill Giant</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-disappearance", "title": "Dust of Disappearance", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This fine, sand-like powder comes in a quantity sufficient for one use. When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to throw the dust into the air, you and each creature and object within a 10-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> condition for 2d4 minutes. The duration is the same for all subjects, and the dust is consumed. Immediately after an affected creature makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell, the condition ends for that creature.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-dryness", "title": "Dust of Dryness", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This small packet holds 1d6 + 4 pinches of dust. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can sprinkle a pinch over water to turn up to a 15-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-cube\">Cube</a> of it into a marble-sized pellet that floats or rests nearby and weighs almost nothing. A creature can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to smash the pellet on a hard surface, shattering it and releasing the water; this destroys the pellet and ends its magic.</p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can also sprinkle a pinch on an Elemental within 5 feet of you that's composed mostly of water, such as a Water Elemental or Water Weird. The creature makes a DC 13 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 10d6 Necrotic damage on a failure or half as much on a success.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dust-of-sneezing-and-choking", "title": "Dust of Sneezing and Choking", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>Found in a small container, this powder resembles Dust of Disappearance, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-identify\">Identify</a> reveals it as such. There is enough for one use. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can throw the dust into the air, forcing you and every creature in a 30-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from you to make a DC 15 Constitution <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>. Constructs, Elementals, Oozes, Plants, and Undead succeed automatically.</p><p>On a failed save, a creature sneezes uncontrollably, has the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> condition, and is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-suffocation\">suffocating</a>. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The effect also ends on a creature targeted by <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-lesser-restoration\">Lesser Restoration</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-elemental-gem", "title": "Elemental Gem", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>This gem holds a mote of elemental energy. When you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to break it, an elemental is summoned (stat blocks are in the Monster Manual) and the gem stops being magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. It disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>.</p><table class=\"humanoid-grid\"><thead><tr><th>Gem</th><th>Summoned Elemental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blue sapphire</td><td>Air Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Emerald</td><td>Water Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Red corundum</td><td>Fire Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Yellow diamond</td><td>Earth Elemental</td></tr></tbody></table>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eversmoking-bottle", "title": "Eversmoking Bottle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can open or close this bottle. Opening it releases thick smoke that fills a 60-foot <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-emanation\">Emanation</a> originating from the bottle, and the area within is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-heavily-obscured\">Heavily Obscured</a>. Each minute the bottle stays open, the Emanation grows by 10 feet, up to a maximum of 120 feet. Closing the bottle fixes the cloud in place until it disperses after 10 minutes. A strong wind, such as one from <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-gust-of-wind\">Gust of Wind</a>, disperses it after 1 minute.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-charming", "title": "Eyes of Charming", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes and have 3 charges. While wearing them, you can expend 1 or more charges to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-charm-person\">Charm Person</a> (save DC 13): 1 charge casts it at level 1, and each additional charge raises the spell's level by 1. The lenses regain all expended charges daily at dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-minute-seeing", "title": "Eyes of Minute Seeing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, your vision improves out to 1 foot, giving you <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> within that range and Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to examine something within it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-eyes-of-the-eagle", "title": "Eyes of the Eagle", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. In clear conditions, you can make out details of even very distant creatures and objects as small as 2 feet across.</p><h5>Legacy Version</h5><p>In the 2014 rules the eyes require attunement; the benefits are otherwise the same.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-silver-raven", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Silver Raven)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This silver statuette of a raven can become a Raven for up to 12 hours, then can't be used again until 2 days have passed. While it is in raven form, the figurine lets you cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-animal-messenger\">Animal Messenger</a> on it.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-rare", "title": "Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-amulet-of-health", "title": "Amulet of Health", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>Your Constitution score is 19 while you wear this amulet. It has no effect on you if your Constitution is already 19 or higher.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bead-of-force", "title": "Bead of Force", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This small black sphere is 3/4 of an inch across; 1d4 + 4 of them are usually found together. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a>, you can throw the bead up to 60 feet. It explodes on impact and is destroyed. Each creature within 10 feet of where it landed makes a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 5d4 Force damage on a failure. A transparent sphere of force then fills the area for 1 minute. A creature that failed the save and is completely inside is trapped; one that succeeded, or is only partly inside, is pushed out. Only breathable air passes through the sphere's wall; no attack or other effect does. A trapped creature can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to push against the wall and move the sphere up to half its Speed. The sphere can be picked up and weighs only 1 pound regardless of what's inside.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-hill-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Hill Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 21. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-levitation", "title": "Boots of Levitation", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-levitate\">Levitate</a> on yourself at will.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-boots-of-speed", "title": "Boots of Speed", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear these boots, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a> to click the heels together. This doubles your Speed, and <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-opportunity-attacks\">Opportunity Attacks</a> made against you have Disadvantage. When you click your heels again, the effect ends. Once the boots' property has been used for a total of 10 minutes, it stops working until you finish a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-long-rest\">Long Rest</a>.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bowl-of-commanding-water-elementals", "title": "Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While this 3-pound bowl, about a foot across and half as deep, is filled with water, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to speak its command word and summon a Water Elemental as though you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a>. The bowl can't be used this way again until the next dawn. It holds about 3 gallons.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-bracers-of-defense", "title": "Bracers of Defense", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing these bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class if you are wearing no armor and using no Shield.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-brazier-of-commanding-fire-elementals", "title": "Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While a fire burns in this brass brazier, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to speak its command word and summon a Fire Elemental as though you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a>. The brazier can't be used this way again until the next dawn. It weighs 5 pounds.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cape-of-the-mountebank", "title": "Cape of the Mountebank", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This cape smells faintly of brimstone. While wearing it, you can use it to cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-dimension-door\">Dimension Door</a>. This property can't be used again until the next dawn. When you disappear, you leave behind a cloud of smoke, and you appear in a similar cloud at your destination. The smoke lightly obscures both spaces and dissipates at the end of your next turn. A light or stronger wind disperses it.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-censer-of-controlling-air-elementals", "title": "Censer of Controlling Air Elementals", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>While incense burns in this 1-foot-wide censer, you can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to speak its command word and summon an Air Elemental as though you had cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-conjure-elemental\">Conjure Elemental</a>. The censer can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-chime-of-opening", "title": "Chime of Opening", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This hollow metal tube, about a foot long, has 10 charges. As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can strike it while pointing it at an object within 120 feet that can be opened, such as a door, lid, or lock. The chime sounds, and one lock or latch on the object opens unless the sound can't reach it. If no locks or latches remain, the object itself opens. The chime then loses a charge; once the last charge is spent, it cracks and is useless.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-displacement", "title": "Cloak of Displacement", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While you wear this cloak, it projects an illusion that makes you appear to be standing near your actual location, so creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. If you take damage, this property stops working until the start of your next turn. It also stops while you have the <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-restrained\">Restrained</a> condition or otherwise can't move.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-the-bat", "title": "Cloak of the Bat", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this cloak, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks, and in an area of <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-dim-light\">Dim Light</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkness\">Darkness</a> you gain a Fly Speed of 40 feet while holding the edges of the cloak. You can also hang upside down from the ceiling like a bat. While upside down and wearing the cloak, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-polymorph\">Polymorph</a> on yourself, becoming a Bat. You keep your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The cloak can't be used this way again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-daern-s-instant-fortress", "title": "Daern's Instant Fortress", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to place this 1-inch metal cube on the ground and speak its command word. The cube rapidly grows into a fortress that stays until you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to speak a command word dismissing it, which works only if the fortress is empty.</p><p>The fortress is a square tower, 20 feet on a side and 30 feet high, with arrow slits on every side and a battlement on top. Its interior has two floors joined by a ladder that ends at a trapdoor to the roof. When it appears, a small door faces you. The door opens only at your command, which you can give as a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-bonus-action\">Bonus Action</a>, and it is immune to <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-knock\">Knock</a> and similar magic such as a Chime of Opening.</p><p>Each creature in the area where the fortress appears makes a DC 15 Dexterity <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-saving-throw\">saving throw</a>, taking 10d10 Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half as much on a success. Either way, the creature is pushed 5 feet away from the fortress. Objects in the area that aren't worn or carried take the damage and are pushed automatically.</p><p>The tower is made of adamantine, and its magic prevents it from being tipped over. The roof, the door, and each wall have 100 Hit Points, Immunity to damage from nonmagical weapons (excluding siege weapons), and Resistance to all other damage. Only a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-wish\">Wish</a> spell can repair it (this counts as duplicating a spell of level 8 or lower); each casting restores the roof, the door, or one wall to full Hit Points.</p><h5>Legacy Version</h5><p>In the 2014 rules the cube doesn't require attunement. It works as above, using actions in place of Magic actions.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-dimensional-shackles", "title": "Dimensional Shackles", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>You can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to place these shackles on an <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-incapacitated\">Incapacitated</a> creature. They adjust to fit a creature of Small to Large size. Besides working as ordinary manacles, they stop the bound creature from using any extradimensional movement, including teleportation and travel to another plane. They don't stop it from passing through an interdimensional portal. You and any creature you designate when you use the shackles can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to remove them. Once every 30 days, the bound creature can make a DC 30 Strength (Athletics) check; on a success, it breaks free and destroys the shackles.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-bronze-griffon", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Bronze Griffon)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This bronze statuette becomes a Griffon for up to 6 hours. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 5 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-ebony-fly", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Ebony Fly)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This ebony statuette becomes a Giant Fly for up to 12 hours and can be ridden as a mount. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-golden-lions", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Golden Lions)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This gold statuette is a pair of lions that become two Lions for up to 1 hour. Once they have been used, the figurine can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-marble-elephant", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Marble Elephant)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This marble statuette becomes an Elephant for up to 24 hours. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-onyx-dog", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Onyx Dog)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This onyx statuette becomes a Mastiff for up to 6 hours. The mastiff has an Intelligence of 8 and can speak Common. It has <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-darkvision\">Darkvision</a> out to 60 feet and can see <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"condition-invisible\">Invisible</a> creatures and objects within that range. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 7 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-figurine-of-wondrous-power-serpentine-owl", "title": "Figurine of Wondrous Power (Serpentine Owl)", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a pocket-sized statuette. If you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> to throw it to a point on the ground within 60 feet, it becomes a living creature; if the space is occupied or too small, nothing happens. The creature is <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-friendly\">Friendly</a> to you and your allies, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you give no commands, it defends itself but takes no other actions.</p><p>The creature lasts for a duration specific to the figurine, then reverts. It also reverts early if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a> while touching it. After it reverts, the figurine can't be used again until the time in its description has passed.</p><p>This serpentine statuette becomes a Giant Owl for up to 8 hours. You and the owl can communicate telepathically at any distance, as long as you are both on the same plane. Once it has been used, it can't be used again until 2 days have passed.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-folding-boat", "title": "Folding Boat", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Rare</strong></p><p>This 12-inch-long, 6-inch-wide, 6-inch-deep box weighs 4 pounds and floats. It has three command words, each requiring a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>. The first unfolds it into a boat 10 feet long, 4 feet wide, and 2 feet deep, with oars, an anchor, a mast, and a lateen sail; it holds four Medium creatures comfortably. The second unfolds it into a ship 24 feet long, 8 feet wide, and 6 feet deep, with a deck, rowing seats, five sets of oars, a steering oar, an anchor, a deck cabin, and a mast with a square sail; it holds 15 Medium creatures. The third folds it back into a box, which works only if no creatures are aboard. Any cargo within the vessel folds into an extradimensional space. If there isn't enough space for the vessel to unfold, nothing happens.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-very-rare", "title": "Very Rare", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-bag-of-devouring", "title": "Bag of Devouring", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong></p><p>This bag looks like a Bag of Holding but is really the feeding mouth of a huge extradimensional creature; turning it inside out closes the mouth. The creature senses whatever is put inside. Animal or vegetable matter placed entirely within the bag is devoured and lost forever. When part of a living creature goes in (for instance, someone reaching inside), there is a 50 percent chance the creature is pulled in.</p><p>A creature inside the bag can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to try to escape with a successful DC 15 Strength check. Another creature can take a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-utilize\">Utilize action</a> to reach in and pull a creature out with a successful DC 20 Strength check (unless it is pulled in first). A creature that starts its turn inside the bag is devoured and its body destroyed. Inanimate objects can be stored inside, up to a cubic foot of them, but once each day the bag swallows everything in it and spits it out on another plane of existence, at a time and place the DM chooses.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-fire-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Fire Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 25. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-frost-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Frost Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 23. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-stone-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Stone Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 23. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-cloak-of-arachnida", "title": "Cloak of Arachnida", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This fine garment is made of black silk interwoven with faint silvery threads. While wearing it, you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Poison Resistance.</strong> You have Resistance to Poison damage.</p><p><strong>Spider Climb.</strong> You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.</p><p><strong>Web Walker.</strong> You ignore movement restrictions caused by webs, and you can move through them as if they were <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-difficult-terrain\">Difficult Terrain</a>.</p><p><strong>Web.</strong> As a <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-magic-action\">Magic action</a>, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-web\">Web</a> (save DC 13). The web created by the spell fills twice its normal area. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball", "title": "Crystal Ball", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Very Rare</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This crystal ball is about 6 inches across. While touching it, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it, and you don't need the spell's material component.</p>\n"}]}, {"id": "magic-items-wondrous-items-legendary", "title": "Legendary", "html": "", "children": [{"id": "magic-item-belt-of-cloud-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Cloud Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 27. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-belt-of-storm-giant-strength", "title": "Belt of Storm Giant Strength", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>While wearing this belt, your Strength score changes to 29. It has no effect on you if your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-mind-reading", "title": "Crystal Ball of Mind Reading", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This crystal ball is about 6 inches across. While touching it, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it, and you don't need the spell's material component. You can also cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-detect-thoughts\">Detect Thoughts</a> through it, targeting creatures within 30 feet of the Scrying sensor, without needing to concentrate on the spell to maintain it. This ability can't be used again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-telepathy", "title": "Crystal Ball of Telepathy", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This crystal ball is about 6 inches across. While touching it, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it, and you don't need the spell's material component. While you scry with it, you can communicate telepathically with creatures you can see within 30 feet of the sensor, and you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-suggestion\">Suggestion</a> through the sensor on one of them. Once you use the suggestion, you can't do so again until the next dawn.</p>\n"}, {"id": "magic-item-crystal-ball-of-true-seeing", "title": "Crystal Ball of True Seeing", "html": "<p><strong>Wondrous Item, Legendary</strong> (requires attunement)</p><p>This crystal ball is about 6 inches across. While touching it, you can cast <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"spell-scrying\">Scrying</a> (save DC 17) with it, and you don't need the spell's material component. While you scry with it, you also have <a href=\"#\" class=\"gloss-ref\" data-ref=\"glossary-truesight\">Truesight</a> through the sensor, out to 120 feet.</p>\n"}]}]}]};
